window.AKK_AFTER_REBIRTH_I_WAS_FORCED_TO_BECOME_THE_MAFIA_PRINCESS_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_AFTER_REBIRTH_I_WAS_FORCED_TO_BECOME_THE_MAFIA_PRINCESS_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":901,"title":"Chapter 901: 902. One Brooch, I Concede.","paragraphs":["The first day of the Lunar New Year.","Weibo’s hot searches exploded.","#A Million-Yuan Lucky Bag Has Been Won# — Trending!","#Elderly Man from the Mountains Wins One Million# — Trending!","#Has ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍WeTalk Crashed?# — Boiling!","#I Shook for Three Minutes and Only Got Sixty-Eight Cents# — Boiling!","#Longfutong Linked More Than Fifty-Three Million Bank Cards# — Hot!","An official Weibo announcement confirmed that, in a remote mountain village in BS Province, an elderly man had won a million-yuan lucky bag. For privacy reasons, however, his identity had not been disclosed.","The moment the news came out, the comments section erupted.","“Holy crap! One million! An actual million yuan in cash!”","“That old man from the mountains became a millionaire with one casual shake, while I shook for ten minutes and only got five yuan and twenty cents. Is this what they call fate?”","“Be grateful for your five yuan. I only got three. I feel like WeTalk is psychologically manipulating me.”","“You’re all focused on the wrong thing. The real point is Longfutong. How long has it been? Its number of linked bank cards has already shot past fifty-three million. Do you know what that means? It took Taobao seven or eight years to build up its payment users, and Longfutong nearly caught up overnight.”","“Taobao: Is there no justice left in this world? I’ve spent seven or eight years building a payment platform, and they caught up in one night.”","“Looks like Ma Yunyun won’t be getting any sleep tonight.”","“Ma Yunyun: Why am I the one getting splashed when you two are fighting?”","“Seriously, don’t you find this terrifying? WeTalk launched a red-packet campaign and actually tied the two Mas together before pinning them to the ground. That’s absolutely brutal!”","“......”","Hangzhou. Taobao headquarters.","The New Year duty roster was normally divided into shifts. In previous years, only about half the employees would have been working at this time.","But this year, not a single person in the payments department had taken leave. Everyone was in the office.","Even Ma Yunyun himself had come in and was personally watching the real-time data on the giant screen.","Two curves were engaged in a fierce chase.","The blue line represented the number of users who had linked bank cards to their payment platform. After seven or eight years, that number had accumulated to more than eighty million.","The red line represented the number of users who had linked bank cards to Longfutong.","Before New Year’s Eve, the red curve had stood at only one-tenth of the blue one.","But from the period before New Year’s Eve onward, the red line began climbing at an almost vertical angle, as if it had been injected with stimulants.","Ten million. Twenty million. Thirty million...","It kept surging until it passed fifty million.","Today, the red line officially broke through the sixty-million mark, leaving it only a little more than twenty million behind the blue line.","“We’ve been doing this for seven or eight years.”","“They caught up in a single Spring Festival.”","Ma Yunyun watched as the members of the payments team sat in silence, their expressions complicated. But he did not blame them.","“I don’t blame any of you.”","“Wanlong Group’s Spring Festival Gala red-packet campaign was indeed an ingenious move. It caught us completely off guard, and it’s absolutely worth studying and reflecting on.”","“President Ma, could we launch a similar campaign?” the head of the marketing department asked.","Ma Yunyun shook his head. “We could, but it would have to wait until next Spring Festival. Doing it now wouldn’t mean anything. They already control the pace.”","He paused, then suddenly let out a laugh. “I, Ma Yunyun, have worked in the internet industry for so many years, and this is the first time someone has beaten me so thoroughly that I couldn’t even fight back. That Liu Yutong really is a genius. I concede.”","Everyone present exchanged glances.","Who was Ma Yunyun?","He was the madman universally acknowledged by the internet industry. When he was running Alibaba, he had dared to go head-to-head with eBay. When he entered the payments industry, he had dared to challenge the banks.","The entire business world of Longguo probably couldn’t produce a second person who could make him say, “I concede.”","“Technical team, listen up.”","“Here!”","“Starting tomorrow, put all your effort into developing a red-packet function. The features must be comprehensive, the experience must be smooth, and the interface must be stable. We must be able to do everything WeTalk can do—and whatever WeTalk can’t do, we must find a way to do as well.”","“Yes!”","Ma Yunyun took one last look at the red line still shooting upward on the giant screen, then turned and left the war room.","In the corridor, he pulled out his phone and opened WeTalk. He stared at the blue-green globe icon for a long time.","Then he held down the icon and tapped Uninstall.","After uninstalling it, he stood there silently for ten seconds before downloading WeTalk again from the app store.","Forget it. He’d give Liu Yutong some face.","............","Shencheng. GooseChat headquarters.","The ashtray on Pony Ma’s desk was already stuffed with cigarette butts, and the air was thick with tobacco smoke.","Pony Ma normally didn’t smoke much, but today he had already gone through more than half a pack.","On the computer screen before him were the figures sent over by his subordinates.","On New Year’s Eve, GooseChat had barely managed to gain five million new users.","Under normal circumstances, that would have been an excellent result. But compared with WeTalk’s more than forty million new users, those five million looked completely insignificant.","And if they counted from when WeTalk began its Five Blessings collection campaign before New Year’s Eve, its growth was far more than forty million.","Looking at the number of new users, Pony Ma suddenly felt like laughing.","A little over a month ago, Liu Yutong had told him, “Within two months, WeTalk’s user base will exceed GooseChat’s by at least thirty million.”","At the time, he had thought that goal was impossible.","Now, only a month and a half had passed, and the gap had probably already exceeded the target by nearly twice that amount.","“President Ma.”","The secretary entered carrying a cup of hot tea. “You haven’t slept all night. Why don’t you get some rest?”","“No need. How far has the data been updated?”","“WeTalk has just released its latest figures. Its total number of registered users has surpassed 120 million.”","Pony Ma nodded. “Got it. You can leave.”","After the secretary left, he was once again alone in the office.","Pony Ma took out the dark-gold invitation to the Dark Phoenix Society and examined it for a long time. At last, he opened it and removed the letter and the token inside.","The letter itself was nothing special. It merely contained the invitation.","The important item was the token—a brooch.","The brooch was only about the size of a thumb, and its design was identical to the black phoenix on the letter: wings spread, head lowered, red eyes glaring.","He had no idea what material it was made of, but it felt surprisingly heavy in his hand.","Pony Ma stared at the brooch for a long time.","Finally, he picked up his phone and sent Liu Yutong a text message.","It contained only five words.","I lost. I’ll fly over tomorrow.","............","The morning of the first day of the New Year.","When Liu Yutong received Pony Ma’s text, she was back in her hometown setting off fireworks with Yaya.","Yaya was wearing a red padded jacket and clutching a handful of sparklers. She hopped and bounced around in the open space. Even though fireworks were nowhere near as beautiful in the daytime as they were at night, she was still having the time of her life.","“Big Sister, what do you think the Nian beast looks like?” Yaya asked, turning around while waving her sparkler.","“Probably like a really, really big dog.”","“Then why is it afraid of firecrackers?”","“Because firecrackers are too loud. Its ears can’t stand them.”","“Oh...” Yaya suddenly understood. “So the Nian beast isn’t actually bad. Its ears are just bigger, so it’s more afraid of loud noises?”","Liu Yutong laughed.","“That’s right. The Nian beast isn’t bad. Its ears are just bigger, and it’s more sensitive to loud sounds.”","“Then I won’t call it the Nian beast anymore. I’ll call it Big Dog Whose Ears Hate Loud Noises.”","Yaya was very pleased with the new name she had chosen for herself. She raised the spent sparkler and began running around the courtyard again.","Watching her little figure dart back and forth, Liu Yutong couldn’t help reminding her, “Be careful. Don’t fall.”","Just then, the phone in her pocket vibrated.","She pulled it out and saw a text message on the screen.","It contained only a few simple words.","[I lost. I’ll fly over tomorrow.]","After reading the message, Liu Yutong calmly slipped the phone back into her pocket, then waved to Yaya.","“Yaya, come here. I’ll show you how to set off a big one.”","“What big one?”","Liu Yutong found a cylindrical firework inside the house and placed it on the stone slab in the middle of the courtyard. Then she crouched down and lit the fuse with a lighter.","The fuse hissed and burned as the sisters backed away several steps together.","Three seconds later, a silver burst of light shot from the firework and exploded into a huge golden flower.","Then came a second burst, followed by a third... Silver and red fireworks continued exploding in succession above the courtyard, creating a breathtaking display.","“Wow!”","“Big Sister, these fireworks are so beautiful! What are they called?”","“These are called ‘A Courtyard Full of Red.’”"]},{"number":902,"title":"Chapter 902: 903, Sign the Letter of Intent","paragraphs":["The second day of the Lunar New Year, in Mingzhu City.","When Pony Ma’s private car pulled up in front of Shunchang Tower, he glanced out the window and froze.","The entrance to Shunchang Tower was packed with people.","They were all dressed in identical black suits, each wearing the same silver dragon-shaped badge. From the entrance all the way to the roadside, they stood in two perfectly orderly rows—at least two or three hundred of them.","With that kind of spectacle and oppressive presence, anyone who didn’t know better might have thought a foreign head of state had come for a visit.","The corner of Pony Ma’s mouth twitched.","He couldn’t tell whether Liu Yutong had arranged such an elaborate welcome for him or was trying to give him a show of force.","Probably both.","“P-President Ma, we’re here,” the driver said cautiously.","Pony Ma took a deep breath and pushed open the door.","The moment he stepped out, the two rows of men in black turned their heads in perfect unison. Hundreds of eyes landed on him at once.","For one brief moment, Pony Ma seriously considered sitting right back down in the car.","Just then, there was movement by the entrance to Shunchang Tower.","Liu Yutong came out to greet him.","She was wearing another black suit today, with that distinctive solid-gold dragon-shaped badge pinned to her chest. Her long hair fell loosely over her shoulders, and a faint smile rested on her face.","Yun Cheng and Lan Die followed half a step behind her. Behind them was a group of core members wearing platinum-colored badges, every one of them carrying an extraordinary air.","“President Ma, Happy New Year,” Liu Yutong said as she approached and extended her hand.","Pony ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍Ma hurried forward and took it. “Director Liu, Happy New Year. This reception of yours... I’m honestly overwhelmed by the honor.”","“President Ma is an esteemed guest. It’s only proper.” Liu Yutong smiled faintly and gestured toward the building. “Please, come inside.”","The two of them walked into Shunchang Tower side by side, followed by the rows of men in black.","As he walked, Pony Ma couldn’t help reflecting to himself.","He had been dealing with Liu Yutong for quite some time, but every meeting with her managed to shock him all over again.","The elevator rose all the way to the forty-eighth floor.","When the conference-room door opened, several people were already inside.","Zhang Dalong, head of WeChat and one of the central figures in the merger negotiations.","Zhao Tianyi, chief legal officer of the Wanlong Association Group, wearing his trademark gold-rimmed glasses.","The other two were the heads of legal and finance who had flown in ahead of time from Big Goose. They were both Pony Ma’s trusted aides, and at that moment they sat stiffly upright.","They hadn’t expected the Wanlong Association headquarters to be this intimidating. Everywhere they looked, there were men in black.","“President Ma, please take a seat.” Liu Yutong sat down at the head of the table.","Pony Ma took the seat opposite her. One glance at the documents on the table was enough for him to understand roughly what was coming.","“President Ma, what do you have to say about the bet we made before?” Liu Yutong asked.","Pony Ma gave a bitter laugh. “Director Liu, there’s nothing left to say. I concede. And I concede wholeheartedly.”","Even now, thinking about that bet made his face burn with embarrassment.","Two months earlier, Liu Yutong had told him that WeChat would surpass GooseChat by thirty million users within two months.","At the time, he had thought the woman must be out of her mind. GooseChat had the enormous traffic pool of QQ behind it. The difference between the two platforms was only a few million users. How could WeChat possibly open up a thirty-million-user lead in just two months?","And then what happened?","Liu Yutong threw ten billion yuan into a Spring Festival red-envelope campaign, and the entire country went crazy.","On New Year’s Eve, Pony Ma had watched with his own eyes as WeChat’s new-user curve shot upward at an almost vertical angle. There was no stopping it.","When he checked the results on the morning of the first day of the new year, WeChat’s registered users had soared to 120 million, while GooseChat was still hovering around sixty million.","What was even more outrageous was that the red-envelope campaign had also managed to knock Old Ma flat in the process.","LongPay’s number of users with linked bank cards had surged by tens of millions over the course of the holiday. The defensive moat that Taobao had spent seven or eight years building had nearly been blasted flat by a single Spring Festival campaign.","Honestly, Pony Ma even felt a little sorry for Old Ma.","The man had only wanted to watch the show from the sidelines. He hadn’t provoked anyone or done anything wrong.","“President Ma, you’re being too serious. Business competition is like that. Sometimes you win, sometimes you lose. It’s perfectly normal.” Liu Yutong turned and nodded at Zhao Tianyi. “Tianyi, let’s begin.”","Zhao Tianyi adjusted his gold-rimmed glasses, opened the thick stack of documents in front of him, cleared his throat, and began reading through the key clauses of the merger agreement one by one.","“Clause One: WeChat will retain independent brand operations, while GooseChat will be incorporated into WeChat.”","Pony Ma nodded slightly.","They had already reached a consensus on this point. Once WeChat was folded into Big Goose, there would be no reason to keep GooseChat. Otherwise, it would simply be a waste of resources.","“Clause Two: Mr. Zhang Dalong will continue to serve concurrently as president of the WeChat division and report to the board of directors of Big Goose Group. The WeChat team will retain an independent organizational structure, with its offices located in Mingzhu City.”","At this, Pony Ma couldn’t help giving Zhang Dalong a long, deep look.","He regretted more than ever letting this man leave back then. If Zhang Dalong were still at Goose Factory, how could any of this have happened? WeChat might have been his product by now.","Of course, he had no idea that Zhang Dalong had also been in an extremely difficult position at the time.","“Clause Three: The Wanlong Association Group will contribute all of WeChat’s assets, along with an additional cash investment, in exchange for a thirty-percent stake in Big Goose Group, thereby becoming its largest shareholder.”","Pony Ma’s eyelid twitched violently.","Thirty percent.","He understood better than anyone what that figure meant.","Big Goose’s ownership structure was already highly dispersed. Nanfei, the foreign corporation, held more than thirty percent. He and several members of the founding team held only a little over ten percent combined, while the rest consisted of scattered shares traded on the secondary market.","Now Liu Yutong was suddenly going to become the largest shareholder. That meant Nanfei would have to give way—or even be forced out entirely.","More importantly, who knew whether The Young Lady would go completely mad and continue buying up shares on the secondary market, increasing her stake step by step until she achieved outright control?","If that happened, he really would be finished.","But that was a problem for later. He had lost the bet, and when you lost, you had to accept it.","For now, all he could do was find a way to place restrictions in the agreement and prevent her from increasing her stake without limits.","Of course, it was still too early to discuss that.","“Director Liu, how do you intend to deal with Nanfei?”","That was exactly the question Liu Yutong had been waiting for.","“Since you’re here, President Ma, I’ll be direct. I’d like to ask you to personally invite the people from Nanfei to come to Mingzhu City.”","“Tell them you’re inviting them to watch the Longteng Cup final on the day of the Lantern Festival.”","Pony Ma: “...”","Invite them to watch a match?","Looking at the smile on her face, Pony Ma suddenly felt a chill run down his back. Surely this woman wasn’t planning to seize control by force?","“Director Liu, you’re not thinking of...”","“Don’t worry, President Ma. We’re a legitimate private enterprise. We never do anything illegal.”","“I merely want to give our foreign friend an up-close experience of the Wanlong Association’s corporate culture. That’s all.”","Corporate culture.","When those four words came from Liu Yutong’s mouth, Pony Ma found them unnerving no matter how he interpreted them.","He couldn’t help recalling the rumors about the Ten Thousand Dragons Society—stories about fleets of hundreds of identical luxury sedans, thousands of men in black surrounding powerful underworld figures, and people being forced to jump from buildings in front of the police...","Forget it. No point thinking about it.","The more he thought about it, the harder it would be to fall asleep.","Pony Ma finally agreed. “All right. I’ll contact him as soon as I get back and ask him to come over.”","It wasn’t as if he was the one playing the villain. He was only passing along a message.","Liu Yutong nodded. “Tianyi, continue.”","Zhao Tianyi pushed up his glasses and went on reading the remaining clauses.","“Clause Four: Mr. Ma will continue to serve as chairman and CEO of Big Goose Group, and his authority over the company’s day-to-day operations and management will not be interfered with.”","Pony Ma felt slightly relieved when he heard this.","At least on the surface, he would still be the captain of Big Goose. He would still have his hands on the wheel.","But before he could fully relax, Zhao Tianyi immediately read the next clause.","“Clause Five: Ms. Liu Yutong undertakes never to increase her shareholding. However, as the largest shareholder, she will have veto power over major strategic decisions.”","Pony Ma’s expression instantly became a sight to behold.","“You call that not interfering with day-to-day operations? You even want veto power!”","“I’m only making sure no one takes advantage of you. That’s called supervision,” Liu Yutong said matter-of-factly.","“What are you supervising?”","“Making sure you don’t make foolish decisions.”","Liu Yutong casually gave him a few examples. “For instance, how Big Goose nearly sold QQ for one million back then. Or how your company actually dared to pay employees in cryptocurrency. And the whole forced either-or fiasco... Haven’t you people made enough foolish decisions already?”","Pony Ma: “...”","He wanted to argue, but every one of those things had really happened.","Zhao Tianyi continued reading the clauses that followed.","There were anti-dilution protections, preemptive subscription rights, arrangements for board seats, and more. Each provision was laid out in meticulous detail, leaving no loopholes unaddressed.","The more Pony Ma listened, the more alarmed he became.","This agreement had taken every possible loophole into consideration. There was no way their legal team could have drafted something so comprehensive without preparing for several months.","In other words, Liu Yutong hadn’t set her sights on Big Goose on a whim. She had been plotting this for a long time.","After all the clauses had been read, Zhao Tianyi closed the document and said calmly, “If neither of you has any objections, you may sign.”","Pony Ma picked up the pen and paused for several seconds over the signature line.","Once he signed, Big Goose would change forever.","The empire he had founded and painstakingly managed for more than a decade would now have another, even more formidable major shareholder.","But in the end, he gritted his teeth and signed his name with a series of quick strokes.","Liu Yutong took the pen and signed her name as well.","The two exchanged the documents and signed them again.","Zhang Dalong, Zhao Tianyi, and the legal and financial representatives from Big Goose then signed in turn.","Of course, what they were signing for the moment was only a letter of intent. Nan Fei’s shares had yet to be acquired, and given the significance of the matter, everything had to remain confidential at this stage.","Only after the situation with Nan Fei had been completely settled would the agreement officially take effect.","Still, this marked a crucial first step.","From this day forward, it could be said that Liu Yutong had effectively taken control of most of Long Kingdom’s internet industry.","Liu Yutong stood and extended her hand toward Pony Ma. “President Ma, we’re family from now on.”","Pony Ma shook her hand, his smile somewhat strained. “Director Liu, I’ll be counting on your guidance from now on.”","“Of course.”","Liu Yutong released his hand, then suddenly thought of something.","“Oh, right, President Ma. When Nan Fei’s largest shareholder arrives, please come along and help receive him. After all, you’ve worked together for so many years. It would be more appropriate for you to be there.”","Pony Ma: “...”","Receive him? What kind of reception was this?","Why didn’t she receive the person she had invited herself? Why did she have to drag him into it?","A sudden, ominous feeling came over him.","Something major was bound to happen on the day of the Lantern Festival."]},{"number":903,"title":"Chapter 903: 904. Van der Burgh Arrives","paragraphs":["On the seventh day of the Lunar New Year, with the festive atmosphere still lingering, the internet industry had already exploded.","Big Goose Group’s stock price entered free fall. From HK$280 billion before New Year’s Eve, it plunged through HK$200 billion within just a few trading days, then dropped again to HK$160 billion. Its market capitalization had nearly been cut in half, dragging the entire Hong Kong technology sector down with it and leaving investors everywhere in despair.","Panic spread throughout the market.","The reason was actually quite simple.","After ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‍WeTalk’s massive red-envelope campaign on New Year’s Eve, everyone had realized one thing: Big Goose was probably never going to catch up with WeTalk in the mobile-social arena.","This wasn’t a matter of being slightly behind. It was an entirely different dimension.","WeTalk’s registered users had soared to 130 million, with daily active users holding steadily above 40 million. GooseChat, meanwhile, was still struggling around the 60-million mark.","Even more disastrous was the fact that GooseChat users spent only one-fifth as much time on the app each day as WeTalk users.","One-fifth.","What did that mean?","It meant that even when users reluctantly installed GooseChat on their phones, they rarely opened it. And when they did, they would take a quick glance before closing it again. There was simply no chance of building any real social engagement.","The capital markets had always voted with their feet. The moment investors sensed that the wind was changing, they began selling off their holdings regardless of the cost. Big Goose’s stock plunged like a kite with a severed string, without even the slightest meaningful rebound.","“Big Goose Is Finished!”","Those four words had practically become the headline of every financial newspaper.","“The Mobile-Social Landscape Is Settled: The Twilight of the Big Goose Empire Has Arrived.”","“WeTalk Ascendant, GooseChat Forced Out.”","“Pony Ma’s Waterloo: From Four Hundred Billion to One Hundred Sixty Billion in Just Six Months.”","One bearish headline after another flooded the media.","At Big Goose’s headquarters in Shencheng, the executives looked utterly dispirited. Every meeting was shrouded in a dead, gloomy silence.","Pony Ma, however, remained surprisingly calm. He showed up at the office on time every day, held his meetings, signed his documents, and carried on as though the storm of negative coverage had nothing to do with him.","Only his secretary and a handful of trusted aides knew that Pony Ma had already reached a private agreement with Liu Yutong of the Wanlong Association.","During the days when Big Goose’s stock had fallen to its lowest point, a rumor suddenly began circulating through investment circles.","The Wanlong Association Group intended to acquire all the shares held by Big Goose’s largest shareholder, Nanfly Capital, and take control of Big Goose as its new largest shareholder.","Once the news broke, the financial world erupted again.","“Wanlong Association is going to acquire Big Goose? Am I reading this right? What kind of legendary company is Wanlong Association? First, they crushed Fruit, and now they’re going to swallow Big Goose whole?”","“You’re leaving someone out. They also took Ma Yun’s payment business down a peg.”","“Fruit: What did I ever do to you? Big Goose: I didn’t do anything to you either! Some Treasure: I was just passing by to watch the show. How did I end up covered in blood too?”","“Hilarious. Is Wanlong Association planning to beat up the entire Dragon Nation internet and technology industries? Who’s next? Baidu? NetEase?”","“I’m more curious about where Wanlong Association gets all its money. Ten billion yuan in red envelopes, and acquiring Big Goose’s shares would cost at least tens of billions. Do they print money? They’re ridiculously rich.”","“Don’t forget what Wanlong Association actually does. They’re a perfectly respectable private enterprise. (Dog-head emoji for self-preservation.)”","“As someone from Jinchuan, I can confirm that this company is extremely... respectable.”","“Those black-clad fighters from Wanlong Association are terrifying. I heard they sent thousands of people into Jinchuan and wiped out the local crime boss.”","“Thousands of people... Is this a private enterprise or a criminal organization?”","“Either way, don’t provoke Wanlong Association. Seriously. They’re terrifying.”","“...”","While the domestic internet was still buzzing with heated discussion, thousands of miles away in Amsterdam, at the headquarters of Nanfly Capital, its chairman, the Dutch investor Vanderberg, was sitting in his office and studying a document before him.","It was a formal acquisition offer sent by Wanlong Association Group.","Vanderberg was fifty-seven years old. Born into an old Dutch investment family, he had spent more than twenty years making his way through the Eastern Continent’s markets. He had begun investing in Big Goose back when it was still a small company with only a few dozen employees, and had watched it grow into a Chinese internet giant. The shares he had initially purchased for tens of millions of U.S. dollars were now worth hundreds of billions of Hong Kong dollars.","The investment had been named one of the most successful cases in the history of venture capital in the Eastern Continent by the Financial Times.","Now, someone wanted to use a few hundred billion Hong Kong dollars to rip this cash cow out of his hands by the roots.","It was laughable.","“Ridiculous!”","Vanderberg tossed the document onto the desk, then summoned the head of Nanfly Capital’s Eastern Continent operations.","“Reply to Wanlong Association. Nanfly Capital will not sell a single share of Big Goose. We believed in this company twenty years ago, we still believe in it now, and we’ll continue to believe in it in the future. No matter how much Wanlong Association offers, we won’t sell.”","The executive across from him hesitated before speaking cautiously.","“Chairman, Wanlong Association’s offer is actually at a considerable premium to the current market price. Considering Big Goose’s present stock-price trend and market expectations...”","“Market expectations?”","Vanderberg let out a cold laugh.","“The market expects Big Goose to collapse, and you believe it? The market once expected Amazon to fail too. Look at it now.”","The executive had nothing to say.","Vanderberg rose and walked over to the floor-to-ceiling window. With his hands clasped behind his back, he gazed at Amsterdam’s gray winter sky.","“I’ve invested in the Dragon Nation for twenty years. I’ve met all kinds of people. Some tried to pressure me through connections. Some tried to overwhelm me with money. Others tried to frighten me with underhanded tactics. But in the end, not one of them managed to take something from me that I didn’t want to sell.”","“Wanlong Association—a company founded less than four years ago—wants to acquire my stake in Big Goose? Ha.”","“Let them take their first company public before they start talking.”","“Also, have someone prepare the private jet. I’m going to the Dragon Nation.”","The executive from the Eastern Continent operations department froze.","“You’re going to the Dragon Nation?”","“Yes.”","Vanderberg nodded.","“The Young Lady of Wanlong Association had Pony Ma personally send me an invitation to attend some... Longteng Cup final. I’d like to see for myself exactly what kind of person this young woman is—the one who has thrown the entire Dragon Nation internet industry into chaos. Her appetite is certainly enormous.”","At the same time, at Big Goose’s headquarters in Shencheng, Pony Ma hung up after receiving Vanderberg’s transoceanic call. His expression was complicated.","Vanderberg’s attitude had been even more unyielding than he had expected.","“Pony, I know you’re under tremendous pressure right now, but Nanfly isn’t some retail investor who runs at the first sign of a falling stock price. We’ve worked together for so many years. You should know my style. If Wanlong Association wants to acquire our shares, they can dream on!”","Vanderberg had even comforted Pony Ma in return, telling him that he would fly to the Dragon Nation in a few days to deal with the matter personally. Pony Ma had nothing to worry about. Nanfly would always be Big Goose’s staunchest supporter.","Its staunchest supporter.","Pony Ma nearly lost his composure the second he heard those words.","That shield of yours is probably no match for the other guy's spear!","To this day, Vanderberg still has no idea that Pony Ma himself is one of the hidden masterminds pulling the strings behind this acquisition.","\"What a mess I've gotten myself into!\" Pony Ma leaned back in his chair, pinching the space between his brows.","He felt as if he was being roasted over an open fire.","On one side was Vanderberg's long-standing trust in him, and on the other was the signed letter of intent for the merger that Liu Yutong held in her hands.","Worst of all, he was the one who had to personally coax Vanderberg over to Mingzhu City, while the man had not the slightest clue what was waiting for him there.","After hesitating for a long time, Pony Ma finally picked up his phone and sent Liu Yutong a text message.","[Vanderberg is being very stubborn, but he's agreed to come to Mingzhu City for the Dragon Soaring Cup.]","Less than thirty seconds later, a reply popped up.","[Got it. Great work, Mr. Ma. Once he's here, he'll naturally agree to the terms.]","Reading those words, Pony Ma felt a chill run down his spine.","He had the distinct feeling that he was leading an old friend he'd worked with for years straight into a trap. But there was no turning back now. That signed letter of intent was his token of allegiance, and he'd already put his name to it — there was no way he dared to back out now.","\"Vanderberg, Vanderberg... don't hold this against me...\"","Pony Ma lit a cigarette, took a slow drag, and exhaled the smoke. \"Once you get to Mingzhu City, you'll understand. Some people simply can't be dealt with just by being tough.\"","Several days later at Danan City International Airport.","A Gulfstream G550 private jet slowly touched down on the runway.","When the cabin door opened, Vanderberg stepped down the airstair in a dark gray cashmere coat, followed by the East Regional Director, two assistants, a personal interpreter, and no fewer than seven or eight bodyguards.","Vanderberg was a tall man who habitually held his chin high, carrying the poise and arrogance of an old-school Western investor.","He had fully expected to be greeted on arrival by a horde of menacing men in black, just like the rumors about the Wanlong Society his assistant had dug up online described.","He had even rehearsed a few sharp, sarcastic lines in his head, ready to throw them out the second they met to throw his hosts off balance.","Much to his surprise, though, there were only three cars waiting for him: three ordinary black Mercedes-Benz S-Class sedans, driven by three young men in black suits with silver dragon emblems pinned to their chests.","The drivers looked to be in their early twenties, lean and built, but unfailingly polite. When they saw him, they gave a slight bow and spoke in fluent foreign languages. \"Mr. Vanderberg, welcome to Mingzhu City. The Young Lady has sent us to pick you up.\"","That's it?","Vanderberg sneered to himself.","The rumors were obviously wildly exaggerated. All that talk about convoys of hundreds of Mercedes-Benz and crowds of men in black everywhere — it was all nonsense made up by internet users from Longguo who had clearly never seen the scale of real power.","He climbed into the back of the car, leaned against the plush leather seat, and propped one leg over the other, feeling far more relaxed now.","The car pulled smoothly out of the airport and merged into the highway traffic.","Vanderberg glanced out the window at the city scenery speeding past and casually asked in a foreign language, \"What kind of competition is this Dragon Soaring Cup of yours?\"","The young driver glanced at him in the rearview mirror and smiled. \"It's a martial arts competition, Mr. Vanderberg. It's the Wanlong Society Group's very first annual internal martial arts tournament.\"","\"An internal corporate martial arts tournament?\" Vanderberg raised an eyebrow, nearly laughing out loud.","A legitimate corporation running a martial arts tournament for its staff? It sounded like one of those silly corporate culture events Longguo companies loved to put on, all for show, just a gimmick to drum up so-called team cohesion.","He asked casually, \"How many people are competing in it?\"","\"Roughly ten thousand or so, Mr. Vanderberg,\" the driver answered offhandedly.","???","Vanderberg's leg, which he had propped up, froze mid-motion.","Te... ten thousand people at an internal corporate martial arts tournament?","What kind of company could get ten thousand employees to take part in a fighting competition?","He's got to be making that up.","He was just about to press for more details when the car exited the highway and turned onto a wide six-lane avenue.","A short while later, a massive stadium came into view — the kind that could seat tens of thousands of people.","The entire parking lot surrounding the venue was packed with cars. Vanderberg swept his eyes over them quickly, and saw that almost every single one was a black Mercedes-Benz, lined up row after row across the entire lot. Their license plates had every combination of consecutive numbers and letters imaginable, and there had to be at least a few hundred of them.","The corner of his mouth twitched uncontrollably.","The car pulled to a stop at the stadium's VIP entrance.","The second Vanderberg stepped out, he spotted a familiar figure waiting for him right at the door — Pony Ma.","\"Ma, you're here too?\" Vanderberg said, caught off guard.","The expression on Pony Ma's face was so complicated it looked like he'd been constipated for three days, finally relieved himself, then realized the toilet was clogged.","But he quickly composed himself, put on a bright smile, stepped forward, and shook Vanderberg's hand. \"Mr. Vanderberg, welcome to Mingzhu City. Director Liu specifically asked me to come and keep you company, so you wouldn't get bored watching the competition alone.\"","Vanderberg clapped him on the shoulder and laughed. \"Ma, you look like you haven't been sleeping well. Too much stress lately? Don't worry, I came all the way here to wrap up this Wanlong Society acquisition once and for all. I give you my word, Nanfei won't sell a single share of Big Goose's stock.\"","Pony Ma's smile was more pained than a sob. \"Thanks a lot.\"","Vanderberg then followed Pony Ma and the two men in black toward the VIP passage, walked down the red-carpeted corridor, and pushed open the heavy soundproof door.","The moment he stepped inside the stadium, he froze completely in place, feeling as if he had just fallen straight into an ice cellar."]},{"number":904,"title":"Chapter 904: 905. An Unparalleled Formation","paragraphs":["Vanderberg stood at the entrance to the VIP passageway, staring at the scene before him in utter shock.","Before entering Long Nation, he had secretly looked down on the Wanlong Association. After all, it was a company from Long Nation that had been established less than four years ago. How impressive could it really be... Heh...","But the moment he stepped through the stadium entrance, the expression on his face instantly became this:","ヽ(;゚д゚)ノ!!!","The stadium was packed with people.","This was not a figure of speech. It was a literal sea of people.","More than ten thousand men in black occupied the surrounding stands. They all wore identical black suits and identical silver dragon-shaped badges. Starting from the front rows of the lowest tier, they filled the stands level by level, all the way to the very top. Densely packed, they looked from a distance like a vast black ocean.","Even though none of them were doing anything, the sheer presence they gave off simply by sitting there was enough to scare a timid person into having a heart attack.","Vanderberg suddenly felt that his legs were no longer obeying him. They felt as though they had been filled with cement, leaving him unable to move.","Standing beside him, Pony Ma secretly glanced at Vanderberg's stunned, terrified expression. For some reason, he felt incredibly satisfied.","This was fantastic!","When he had first arrived at the stadium and seen so many people in black, his reaction had been almost identical to Vanderberg's.","Now, at last, someone else could experience the same shock he had felt.","\"Mr. Vanderberg, shall we go in?\"","Vanderberg walked stiffly into the stadium and finally got a clear view of the entire venue.","A huge arena had been constructed right in the center of the stadium.","It was nearly half the size of a basketball court, perfectly square, with a platform standing a little over a meter above the ground. Four enormous LED screens surrounded it on all sides.","Suspended directly above the arena was a circular display screen, where three large characters scrolled across it:","—The Dragon Soaring Cup!","Two couplets hung on either side of the arena.","The first read:","Fists and feet reveal the truth; the dragon soars across the four seas.","The second read:","Law and reason determine the universe; the association gathers heroes from every corner.","After hearing the translator explain the meaning of the couplets, Vanderberg felt deeply unsettled.","They gave him the strange impression of being both righteous and sinister.","The sinister part was that these men in black looked far too much like an overseas criminal organization—and on the surface, they seemed countless times more powerful than even the strongest organizations abroad.","The righteous part was that these people apparently studied the law as well?","It was... an extremely contradictory combination.","\"Mr. Vanderberg, your seat is over here.\" The black-clad staff member responsible for guiding him pointed toward several empty seats in the center of the front row.","Vanderberg nodded and slowly made his way over.","With every step he took, he could clearly feel gazes coming at him from all directions.","There was no malice or murderous intent in those eyes, yet they still made the hair on his body rise involuntarily.","His two assistants and eight bodyguards followed behind him. He had brought those bodyguards from Helan. Every one of them stood over 1.9 meters tall and possessed exceptional fighting skills. They would have had no trouble intimidating ordinary thugs.","But compared with the Wanlong Association's black-clad members surrounding them, he suddenly felt that his own bodyguards looked like a flock of quails in suits.","Any one of these people could crush them to pieces with a casual squeeze.","Moreover, the discipline of the Wanlong Association's members was terrifying. Every one of them sat upright, chests out and backs straight, as motionless as statues.","Vanderberg had spent many years in the business world. He had seen plenty of private security teams, including highly disciplined ones, but he had never seen so many people maintain such terrifying discipline at the same time.","Once again, he remembered the information his assistant had gathered about the Wanlong Association before his departure.","[Wanlong Association Group, founded in 2007, with its headquarters in Pearl City. Its founder and chairwoman is Liu Yutong. The group encompasses six major business divisions: commercial retail, technology, digital services, entertainment and media, supply-chain logistics, and financial investment. It has more than two hundred thousand employees...]","The information was formal and official.","But on the final page, his assistant had added several comments copied from internet forums in Long Nation.","[The Wanlong Association? Isn't that the largest organization in Pearl City... No... the largest organization in all of Long Nation?]","[I heard they mobilized four thousand people in BS Province and completely crushed the local crime lord.]","[...]","At the time, Vanderberg had merely laughed after reading those comments. People from Long Nation loved to exaggerate. They loved to boast.","Now, he could not laugh anymore.","Not even a little.","Finally, under the guidance of the staff, he took his seat.","Pony Ma sat to his left, while the seat to his right remained empty. Clearly, it had been reserved for someone even more important.","Vanderberg had barely sat down and had not yet had time to catch his breath when a golden spotlight suddenly descended vertically from the center of the dome, illuminating the middle of the arena.","Whoosh!","More than twelve thousand black-clad members throughout the stadium rose to their feet almost simultaneously.","Vanderberg was startled once again. He had no idea what was happening.","Pony Ma stood up beside him as well. He gently nudged Vanderberg with his elbow and whispered, \"Mr. Vanderberg, you should stand too. It's a rule of the Wanlong Association. Whenever The Young Lady makes an appearance, everyone must rise.\"","The Young Lady.","There was that title again.","Ever since arriving in Long Nation, Vanderberg had heard it countless times.","He was determined to see for himself exactly what kind of person this Young Lady was—the woman everyone kept mentioning.","The moment he stood up, the stadium's domed wraparound screen lit up.","A golden dragon pattern slowly emerged across the enormous LED screen encircling the entire venue. Its body twisted and coiled, its head held high and its eyes wide open, radiating an imposing might as it looked down upon the entire stadium.","As the dragon pattern appeared, a deep drumbeat echoed through the venue.","Boom!","Boom!","Boom!","Every beat was deep and powerful, shaking the blood in their veins until it surged and boiled.","The drumbeats grew faster and more urgent.","Just as they reached their climax, the northern gates of the stadium suddenly opened.","Dozens of black-clad men wearing platinum-colored badges on their chests stepped out first, then lined up on both sides.","Immediately afterward, a man and a woman walked out side by side, guarding the center.","Finally, behind the two guards, a cold, sharp black figure slowly emerged from the shadows, taking one step after another.","She was an extremely young woman dressed in a custom-made black suit. She possessed an overwhelming aura of supreme power, as though she stood above all living things.","A badge was pinned to her chest as well.","A pure-gold dragon-shaped badge.","The badges worn by all twelve thousand people present were either silver or platinum-colored. She alone wore one made of pure gold.","It displayed her unique and unrivaled position.","The instant she appeared, all twelve thousand people lowered their heads in perfect unison. They clenched their left fists and pressed them against their hearts, shouting:","\"Greetings, The Young Lady!\"","“Hello, Young Lady!” shouted more than ten thousand people.","The deafening roar reverberated throughout the venue. Vanderberg instantly felt as if his eardrums were about to burst.","The seven or eight bodyguards he had brought from Helan stood rigidly beside him, their faces pale and their eyes filled with fear and tension.","Pony Ma was little better. Although he had seen members of the Wanlong Association before, this was his first time witnessing such a spectacular scene in person: more than ten thousand men in black saluting a single person at the same time.","The Big Goose Group also had tens of thousands of employees, but the feeling was completely different from what he was seeing now.","When the Big Goose employees saw him, they merely greeted him with ordinary smiles. These people were different. Through their actions, they were telling you directly that as long as The Young Lady gave the order, they would do anything for her.","Yes, anything!","That almost fanatical loyalty was something no normal company possessed. You could search the entire world and still never find anything like it.","“Take your seats.”","Just two casual words.","All twelve thousand people sat down in perfect unison, like a black tide sinking simultaneously.","At the center of the ring, Liu Yutong held a microphone, her voice carried throughout the entire venue by the surround-sound system.","“First of all, congratulations to the two hundred contestants who emerged victorious from among the tens of thousands of core members across the seven major divisions and made it to the stage of the Longteng Cup finals.”","“Every one of you is a source of pride for the Wanlong Association!”","Thunderous applause erupted, spreading through the venue like a tidal wave.","“Next, I would also like to extend my special thanks to the two guests joining us today.”","“Mr. Ma, chairman of the board of the Big Goose Group.”","Pony ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​‍Ma’s name had barely been called before he hurriedly stood up and nodded slightly to the crowd.","“Mr. Vanderberg, chairman of Nanfei Capital.”","The translator relayed the words to Vanderberg, and he immediately stood up, looking just like an elementary school student being called on by his teacher.","As more than ten thousand pairs of eyes focused on him, his heart nearly stopped beating again.","The pressure was insane!!!","At that moment, Vanderberg finally formed an entirely new opinion of the Wanlong Association.","This was not an ordinary company at all.","This damn well was a... XXX!!!","Just as everyone’s attention was fixed on the stage, Liu Yutong announced that the competition was officially beginning.","“The Longteng Cup finals—begin now!”"]},{"number":905,"title":"Chapter 905: 906. A Fierce Competition.","paragraphs":["Liu Yutong stepped down from the ring and walked straight to the VIP section, taking the main seat on Vanderberg’s right.","From the moment she left the ring until she sat down, she merely gave Vanderberg a slight nod without saying a word. Then she fixed her eyes on the ring in the center of the arena.","The fact that she remained silent only made Vanderberg even more uneasy.","He had already sensed the tremendous pressure radiating from the girl when he first saw her from a distance. Now that she was sitting less than three feet away, that pressure felt as if it were crushing directly against his face.","He couldn’t help sneaking a glance at the pure-gold dragon-shaped badge on her chest. There was no denying that the badge was dazzling. Paired with her exquisite profile and the overwhelming aura she gave off, it was enough to make even an investor who controlled tens of billions of dollars feel short of breath.","“Mr. Vanderberg, watch the match,” Pony Ma reminded him quietly when he noticed his unease.","“Oh... oh, right.” Vanderberg quickly pulled his gaze away and sat up straight.","But he couldn’t concentrate no matter how hard he tried. The corner of his eye kept drifting involuntarily toward his right.","The more this heiress refused to say anything, the more tormented he felt.","What exactly was she planning?","Why had she invited him to watch this match?","Why wasn’t she saying a word?","Boom!","A deep drumbeat interrupted his restless thoughts.","The Dragon Soaring Cup finals had officially begun.","The first event was the men’s bout for third place.","The two fighters came from the East China and Southwest divisions. Both were sturdy young men in their early twenties—one specialized in sanda, while the other practiced traditional martial arts.","The moment they engaged on the ring, they went all out, every punch landing with bone-rattling force. The sight made the crowd’s blood surge.","At the commentary booth, Ma Da picked up his microphone and began his characteristically fiery commentary.","“Brothers and sisters!”","“Standing on the left side of the ring is Lin Xiaohu from the East China division! Lin Xiaohu fought his way into the finals with an eleven-and-zero record during the qualifiers. His signature technique is a series of three low kicks followed by a high roundhouse kick. The brothers jokingly call him the Sweeping Monk, because anyone he sweeps with those kicks ends up sprawled on the ground as cleanly and efficiently as a freshly swept floor!”","“On the right is Peng Dazhuang from the Southwest division! Da Zhuang went ten wins and one loss during the qualifiers. And that one loss happened because he had diarrhea after eating hot pot the day before...”","“Hahahaha!”","The entire arena erupted in laughter.","Vanderberg and the bodyguards around him couldn’t understand a word of Dragonian, but when they saw more than ten thousand people laughing, they twitched their lips and joined in with a few awkward chuckles.","“Begin!”","“Lin Xiaohu launches the first attack! Low kick! Another low kick! And another! Three in a row! Beautiful! Peng Dazhuang’s leg has already been kicked red, but he’s still toughing it out. Is that leg made of iron? No, wait—even iron would be bent out of shape by now...”","“Peng Dazhuang is fighting back! He’s grabbed Lin Xiaohu’s arm! He’s going for a takedown! Lin Xiaohu is struggling desperately! The two are locked in a test of strength! This scene reminds me of when I used to play tug-of-war with the ox at home when I was little. Of course, my ox wasn’t nearly this muscular...”","“Lin Xiaohu has broken free! A swinging punch right into Peng Dazhuang’s face! Peng Dazhuang staggers! Lin Xiaohu takes advantage and follows with a flying knee! Peng Dazhuang is down... Wow!”","“The referee is counting!”","“Ten! Nine! Eight! Seven... Peng Dazhuang is getting up! He’s actually getting up! What kind of medicine did this guy take? How can he be this tough? Wait, he seems to have smiled. Is he enjoying this? Is he a masochist?!”","“Hahahaha!”","The arena once again exploded with laughter.","In the end, Lin Xiaohu won third place in the men’s combat event, while Peng Dazhuang took fourth.","The two fighters bowed to each other in the ring, then walked off with their arms around each other’s shoulders, looking nothing like the men who had just fought as if their lives depended on it.","Next came the women’s bout for third place, which was just as thrilling.","The two female fighters fought even more fiercely than the men. Vanderberg’s eyelids twitched as he watched, and he secretly congratulated himself on being seated in the audience instead of standing in the ring.","However, the first true climax of the event came with the next two competitors.","The men’s combat final.","Yun Cheng versus Chu Yang.","When the two names appeared simultaneously on the giant circular screen, all twelve thousand men in black rose to their feet almost as one and erupted into deafening cheers.","“Brother Yun! Brother Yun! Brother Yun!”","“Brother Yang! Brother Yang! Brother Yang!”","“...”","The supporters split into two mighty camps. One side chanted for Yun Cheng, while the other cheered for Chu Yang. The roar was so loud it nearly tore the roof off the stadium.","Yun Cheng and Chu Yang emerged onto the ring at the same time.","Both wore black training pants and stood bare-chested, their lean, well-proportioned muscles clearly visible.","Yun Cheng’s expression was cold and stern, his gaze as sharp as a blade.","A faint smile played at the corners of Chu Yang’s lips, while an untamed, wolfish aura radiated from his entire body.","Ma Da’s commentary rang out once more, his tone several times more excited than before.","“Brothers! Sisters! A historic moment has arrived!”","“Standing on the left side of the ring is Yun Cheng—Brother Yun—from our Bright Pearl City division! From the beginning of the tournament until now, he has fought thirty-seven matches and advanced almost entirely undefeated!”","“On the right is Chu Yang—Brother Yang—also from our Bright Pearl City division! He too has advanced with an almost perfect record! Since the very first day of the tournament, the two of them have occupied the top two spots on the Ten Thousand Dragons Rankings, trading wins and losses between them!”","“Today, ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍they will finally face off! This is the ultimate showdown of the Dragon Soaring Cup’s inaugural men’s combat event!”","“Brother Yun versus Brother Chu! Will Brother Yun’s explosive power prevail, or will Brother Chu’s crushing pressure prove stronger? Let’s waaaaait and see!”","Boom!","The drum announcing the start of the match sounded.","The entire stadium fell silent in an instant.","All twelve thousand spectators seemed to hold their breath at the same time.","That sudden silence was even more oppressive than the roaring cheers moments earlier. Vanderberg and Pony Ma could practically hear their own hearts pounding—thump, thump, thump, thump—fast and hard.","On the ring, Yun Cheng and Chu Yang moved simultaneously.","The two figures exploded forward and collided. The impact, amplified through the sound system, echoed throughout the stadium.","Their first exchange lasted less than five seconds. Both men retreated two steps and widened the distance between them, their expressions turning grave.","“That was too fast! I couldn’t see a thing! Do we have a replay? Director, do we have a replay?” Ma Da slapped the commentary desk dramatically.","The giant circular screen replayed the exchange in slow motion.","In those brief five seconds, the two men had traded more than a dozen blows. Every punch and kick was fast, vicious, and precise. If either of them had reacted even half a beat too slowly, the other would have knocked him flat.","A collective gasp swept through the arena.","Even though Vanderberg was a layman, he couldn’t help inhaling sharply when he watched the slow-motion replay.","What the fuck kind of combat skill was this?","The seven or eight bodyguards he’d brought from He Lan probably wouldn’t last even two rounds against these two."]},{"number":906,"title":"Chapter 906: 907. The competition continues, legal questions.","paragraphs":["The second exchange began in the arena.","This time, Yun Cheng made the first move. A combination of punches came crashing down on Chu Yang like a torrential storm.","Chu Yang met them calmly, blocking, dodging, and counterattacking without giving up an inch.","“Yun is on the offensive! Chu is defending! Yun’s attacks are absolutely ferocious, like a raging storm! But Chu is steady as well—like a reef standing firm no matter how violent the waves!”","“Chu is counterattacking! A sweeping kick aimed at Yun’s legs! Yun jumped to evade it, and the moment he landed, he grabbed Chu’s shoulder—he’s going for a knee strike! Chu blocked it with his elbow! They’ve separated again!”","“My God! It’s only the second round, and I’m already out of breath! This is way too intense!”","The third round began.","Chu Yang suddenly changed tactics, switching from defensive counterattacks to an all-out offensive. He was like an enraged wild wolf, every punch and kick carrying a savage, fearless brutality.","The barrage of attacks forced Yun Cheng backward again and again until his back was nearly pressed against the ropes at the edge of the ring.","“Chu is finally showing his true strength! Is this his strategy? He conserved quite a bit of energy through his defense earlier, and now he’s finally holding nothing back! ......... Yun has been driven into the corner! Can he withstand this?”","Before he could finish speaking, Yun Cheng suddenly slipped past Chu Yang’s straight punch. At the same time, he seized Chu Yang’s wrist with his left hand, pressed down on his shoulder with his right, and executed a clean, powerful sweep.","In an instant, the momentum shifted from offense to defense.","Chu Yang was twisted to the ground, his back slamming heavily into the mat with a dull thud.","The entire gymnasium fell silent.","The referee rushed forward and began counting.","“One! Two! Three! Four! Five...”","Chu Yang struggled to get back up, but Yun Cheng’s wrist-and-shoulder lock had been too tricky. The moment he fell, he had instinctively tried to roll with the impact, only to jam his own joints even more tightly.","By the time he finally managed to push himself up from the mat, the referee’s count had already reached eight.","“Eight—nine—ten!”","The match was over.","The entire venue remained silent for three full seconds before erupting into thunderous cheers and applause.","“Yun won!!!”","“Yun Cheng is the inaugural Longteng Cup Men’s Combat Champion!!!”","Ma Da was so excited that he nearly fell off the commentary platform. Gripping the microphone, he roared, “This was a clash between two titans! A showdown worthy of being recorded in the annals of the Wanlong Association! Yun has proven with his strength that he remains the strongest man in the Wanlong Association!”","“Of course, aside from that inhuman guy, Ji Yu!”","Ji Yu: “???”","Chu Yang climbed to his feet, shook his numb arm, and walked over to Yun Cheng.","The two men stared at each other for a second before breaking into simultaneous laughter and sharing a solid embrace.","Seeing this, Vanderberg once again subconsciously glanced at Liu Yutong beside him.","The corners of Liu Yutong’s lips lifted slightly, and a trace of pride flashed through her eyes.","Vanderberg had no choice but to admit defeat.","Either of these two men, who had fought so fiercely on the arena that the heavens seemed to turn upside down, would have been an absolute powerhouse anywhere else. Yet before this young woman, both of them displayed absolute obedience and loyalty.","Just how had this woman managed to accomplish that?","Time passed little by little.","The women’s combat final began as well, and Lan Die claimed the championship with an almost overwhelming advantage.","Next came the physical fitness competition...","Once the physical fitness competition ended, the setup on the arena was quickly removed. Two rows of tables and chairs were brought out, along with a massive answer board.","The image on the circular giant screen changed as well. The previous scenes of heated, flesh-and-blood combat were replaced by a new line of large characters.","[Longteng Cup · Law Knowledge Championship]","The black-clad men throughout the venue, who had previously been roaring with excitement, now became filled with intense anticipation.","“Here it comes! This is the event everyone’s been waiting for!” Ma Da’s voice rang out once more.","“Up next is the third event of this year’s Longteng Cup—the Law Knowledge Championship! Before introducing the contestants, let me first explain the rules and the source of the questions.”","“All the questions for this Law Knowledge Championship were jointly prepared by the Wanlong Association Group’s Legal Affairs Department and Tianyi Law Firm. There are thirty questions in total, all multiple-selection questions. Ten points will be deducted for every wrong answer, while every correct answer earns twenty points. The highest possible score is six hundred, and the contestant with the highest final score wins!”","“Now, let us welcome our Chief Archmage...”","“Ahem, I mean, our Chief Attorney—Zhao Tianyi!!!”","A spotlight abruptly shone on a young man in the audience whose face carried a hint of roguishness.","It was Zhao Tianyi.","Zhao ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‍Tianyi pushed up his gold-rimmed glasses, rose with a smile, and walked onto the arena.","Immediately afterward, dozens of contestants who had fought their way through the law-exam rankings of the seven major divisions entered one after another.","Most of them were ordinary core members wearing silver badges. Only a select few had platinum-colored badges pinned to their chests.","The competition officially began.","The host displayed the first question, and Ma Da read it aloud.","“Question One! Zhang San and Li Si got into a verbal altercation. Zhang San picked up a brick from the ground and threw it at Li Si. Under which of the following circumstances does Zhang San’s conduct constitute the crime of intentional injury?”","“A. The brick strikes Li Si in the head, causing a minor concussion.”","“B. The brick strikes Li Si in the arm, causing soft-tissue bruising.”","“C. The brick strikes Li Si’s pet dog, killing it on the spot.”","“D. The brick misses every target but frightens a child watching nearby into tears.”","“E. Before throwing the brick, Zhang San shouts, ‘I’m going to make you bleed today!’ The brick then slips from his hand and flies across the road, smashing the windshield of a police car.”","The entire venue: “...”","After one second of silence, the entire gymnasium erupted in laughter.","“What the hell? This question is ridiculous!”","“What’s with the brick hitting the dog? Hahahaha...”","“Is option E trying to kill me with laughter and inherit my Wanlong Association badge?”","“......”","Vanderberg’s interpreter quickly translated the question for him. The more he translated, the stranger his expression became. By the time he reached option E, even the interpreter couldn’t stop himself from laughing.","Vanderberg: “...”","What the hell kind of company’s internal exam was this?","No matter how he looked at it, this didn’t seem like a legitimate law exam at all.","Before long, Zhao Tianyi was the first to give his answer.","“The correct answers are A and E.”","“Option A requires no further explanation. I’ll focus on option E.”","“When Zhang San carried out the act of violence, he clearly expressed criminal intent. The words he shouted constitute an explicit expression of intent. Although he failed to strike his original target, he smashed the windshield of a police car instead. This constitutes an attempted intentional injury resulting from a mistake regarding the object of the act, and he is still guilty of attempted intentional injury.","“As for damaging the police car, that constitutes the crime of intentionally damaging property. The two offenses are absorbed under the principle of choosing the more serious charge. As for option D, frightening a child into tears does not constitute a crime unless the child develops a mental disorder as a result...”","Everyone: “...”","The contestant: “...”","Vanderberg: “...”","What the hell—this is way too professional?!","But what exactly was the difference between smashing a dog with a brick and...?","Why would anyone come up with such an outrageous question?","And why could he explain such an absurd question in such a serious tone?","Most importantly, why did he get the impression that this guy had the air of some kind of lawless outlaw?"]},{"number":907,"title":"Chapter 907: 908. Making an Offer.","paragraphs":["“Question two.”","“While Zhang San was singing karaoke at a KTV, he got into a confrontation with Li Si from the private room next door. Zhang San picked up a beer bottle from the table and smashed it at Li Si. Under which of the following circumstances might Zhang San’s actions be considered lawful self-defense?”","“A. Li Si first attacked Zhang San with a beer bottle, so Zhang San smashed one back at him.”","“B. Li Si pointed at Zhang San and said, ‘You sing terribly.’ Zhang San, enraged, smashed the bottle at him.”","“C. Li Si was making unwanted advances toward Zhang San’s girlfriend, so Zhang San smashed the bottle at him to protect her.”","“D. Li Si hadn’t done anything, but Zhang San was a member of the Wanlong Association and felt that not smashing him would damage the company’s reputation.”","“E. Li Si turned out to be Zhang San’s long-lost biological brother. The two suddenly recognized each other while smashing beer bottles, then hugged and wept bitterly.”","“Hahahahaha!”","The entire hall erupted in laughter once again. Some people laughed so hard they slapped their thighs, while others were crying.","Only the Wanlong Association could come up with questions like these. You’d never see such bizarre options anywhere else.","Once again, Zhao Tianyi was the first to answer.","“The correct answers are A and C.”","“A is a classic example of defensive counterattack, while C involves defending another person’s personal rights. B does not constitute self-defense, because ‘singing terribly’ does not qualify as an ongoing unlawful assault.","“Although some scholars believe that mental harm should also count as harm, current judicial practice does not support that view.","“Of course, if you smash someone with a bottle just because they said you sing terribly, the court will only conclude that you really do sing terribly—and that you’re not particularly bright either.”","Another wave of laughter swept through the audience.","“Option D is very misleading, so I’d like to take this opportunity to reiterate that the Wanlong Association is a legitimate business.”","“If any of you brothers feel that not smashing someone would damage the company’s reputation, come to the law firm after the competition and speak with me privately.”","The moment he said this, the laughter abruptly stopped.","Nearly all the core members silently looked away, carefully avoiding Zhao Tianyi’s gaze.","Speaking privately with Lawyer Zhao was worse than stepping into the ring and fighting Brother Yun. At least Brother Yun wouldn’t make them copy the Criminal Law ten times.","“As for option E, I’d like to explain that one as well.”","“First ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌‍of all, although suddenly recognizing a relative in the middle of a fight may be touching from an ethical perspective, it is neither a ground that excludes illegality nor a ground that excludes criminal responsibility. Second, if the two really are biological brothers, a criminal settlement may be reached if the injury is minor or less severe, but criminal liability must still be pursued for serious injuries or worse. Finally, I personally recommend against conducting a paternity test in a KTV. The accuracy cannot be guaranteed, and it’s expensive besides.”","“Hahahahaha...”","The hall erupted in laughter for the third time.","Even the black-clad men standing beside the ring to maintain order could no longer keep straight faces. Their shoulders were trembling, and one of them finally lost control and covered his face with his hand.","With the help of the interpreter, Vanderberg struggled to digest both the questions and the answers. The look on his face gradually changed from bewilderment to understanding.","He finally got it.","The Wanlong Association’s legal department had not designed these questions for an examination at all.","They were using the most outrageous scenarios imaginable to teach every member about the law, turning dry legal provisions into hilarious but unforgettable jokes.","And there was no denying that it worked. Even he had become interested.","The earlier display had been a demonstration of brute force. Now they were displaying the power of the law.","Miss Liu’s ability to manage her people was truly astonishing. It was unlike anything he had ever seen.","When necessary, she could be ruthless enough to fight and kill. When rules had to be observed, she understood the law better than anyone.","He had lived for more than fifty years and had never encountered anyone else who could maintain such a remarkable balance—let alone make it work.","Vanderberg could no longer hold back and took the initiative to break the silence.","“Miss Liu, your employees are... quite interesting.”","Liu Yutong finally turned her head and looked directly at him for the first time.","“Mr. Vanderberg, every member of the Wanlong Association has undergone strict screening and training. They may be very capable fighters, but they are equally law-abiding. I believe that whether in our Dragon Country or abroad, obeying the law is the bottom line every citizen should follow. Don’t you agree?”","The corner of Vanderberg’s mouth twitched.","He really did not believe she meant that sincerely.","Law-abiding? He didn’t buy it.","Using loopholes in the law to carry out acts of violence—that, he could believe.","But he would never say that aloud.","“Yes, yes, of course, Miss Liu. You’re absolutely right.”","Liu Yutong smiled.","“So, Mr. Vanderberg, since you agree, tell me this: would you rather face an enemy who completely disregards the law, or have a friend who abides by it?”","Vanderberg: “...”","Damn it. She had put it that way—only an idiot wouldn’t know which one to choose.","The National Legal Knowledge Championship came to an end amid waves of laughter.","There was no suspense about the winner. Zhao Tianyi took first place with 580 out of a possible 600 points.","The only reason he had not received a perfect score was that he had deliberately left the final question unanswered, giving those who came after him a chance to catch up.","Second place went to a black-framed-glasses-wearing young woman, who scored 460 points and emerged as the dark horse of the competition.","Rumor had it that she was a top graduate of the law school at Capital University and was currently interning under Zhao Tianyi at Tianyi Law Firm.","After the legal knowledge competition ended, Liu Yutong glanced at the watch on her wrist and then rose to her feet.","The moment she stood, more than ten thousand people throughout the venue fell silent and rose along with her.","“Mr. Vanderberg.”","Vanderberg shuddered and hurriedly stood as well.","“Yes, Miss Liu!”","Liu Yutong said, “Mr. Vanderberg, thank you for coming all the way from Helan to watch this competition. But I know that you didn’t come to Pearl City just to watch the event.”","Vanderberg’s heart gave a thump.","What was coming had finally arrived.","“Miss Liu, regarding Big Goose’s shares, I’ve already made my position clear to President Ma...”","Liu Yutong raised a hand and cut him off.","“Nan Fei holds roughly thirty percent of Big Goose’s shares. I’m willing to leave you no more than five percent. That is the Wanlong Association’s goodwill. I hope you won’t disappoint us.”","“Also, I’ve heard that Nan Fei has excellent connections and resources in the West, especially in your hometown of Helan. The Wanlong Association is about to make a full-scale push into overseas markets, and we need a partner with a solid foundation in Helan.”","“I think you’d be a suitable choice,” Liu Yutong added.","Vanderberg was stunned.","She was willing to leave him five percent—and wanted to cooperate with him?","He had originally assumed that Liu Yutong intended to swallow all of the shares in his hands. Before coming, he had even prepared himself for a complete falling-out.","But now, not only had she taken the initiative to offer him a portion of the shares, she had also extended an invitation to cooperate.","This was completely different from the script he had imagined.","At the same time, he could not find a single reason to refuse.","Because he knew perfectly well that if the Wanlong Association truly wanted to seize the shares from him by force, he would not stand the slightest chance against their power.","Now that they had taken the initiative to give him a way out and even left him a little something to profit from, refusing to show any gratitude would simply be foolish.","A moment later, Vanderberg extended his hand.","“Miss Liu, I look forward to our cooperation.”","Liu Yutong smiled faintly and shook his hand. “We’ll become good friends, Mr. Vanderberg.”","Pony Ma, who witnessed the scene, wore a complicated expression.","There was relief, emotion, and even the slightest hint of sympathy.","He was relieved that choosing to work with Liu Yutong back then had been the right decision.","He was moved by the realization that this young woman, nearly twenty years younger than him, possessed a level of savvy and vision far beyond anything he had imagined.","And that trace of sympathy was for Vanderberg.","The old fellow probably still had no idea that every step he had taken from beginning to end had been planned in advance by Liu Yutong.","From the Spring Festival Gala red-packet campaign that had taken the world by storm, to Big Goose’s stock-price collapse; from signing the merger letter of intent himself, to personally coaxing Vanderberg to Pearl City; and then to this Longteng Cup, which was enough to keep anyone awake at night—this had been one elaborate trap after another.","Forget it. They were all on the same boat now. Thinking too much would only shorten his life.","Vanderberg stood there, his expression no less colorful.","He had clearly been carved up and made to surrender a sizable chunk of flesh, yet for some reason, he actually felt the slightest urge to thank the other party.","It was almost as if he had been sold and still wanted to thank the person who sold him.","It was utterly absurd!"]},{"number":908,"title":"Chapter 908: 909. Core members enter the overseas market.","paragraphs":["The Longteng Cup Finals came to a close amid a deafening roar of cheers.","After Liu Yutong personally presented the awards to the champions, she announced on the spot that the remaining prize pool of more than ten million yuan would be distributed among all the participating athletes. The entire venue erupted once again.","Once the award ceremony was over, the setup on the arena floor was quickly removed.","Holding a microphone, Liu Yutong stood alone at the very center of the stage, drawing every eye in the venue.","Everyone instinctively held their breath, waiting for her to speak.","“What I’m about to say is very important.”","With that single sentence, Pony Ma and Vanderberg, seated in the front row, straightened in their chairs at exactly the same time.","“It has been nearly four years since the Wanlong Association was founded.”","“Four years ago, when we got started in Wushui County, we had only a dozen people and a beat-up minivan.”","“Today, our core membership has surpassed ten thousand, our official workforce exceeds two hundred thousand, and our operations span six major business divisions across more than a dozen provinces nationwide.”","A low murmur spread through the audience.","Every veteran member wore an indescribable expression, as though remembering the hardships they had endured, or marveling at how unreal everything seemed.","“But it’s still not enough.”","“Over the next five years, the Wanlong Association will officially begin its overseas expansion.”","The entire venue exploded.","The Wanlong Association had actually maintained overseas operations for some time, but its foundation abroad was still shallow. Aside from the capital controlled by Liu Yutong, only Longyao Mobile and WeChat had established a presence in overseas markets.","Moreover, those operations were largely run by ordinary local employees they had hired. The organization’s core members had never ventured abroad on a large scale.","This time, Liu Yutong was not merely sending a few business representatives overseas. She intended to select people from among the core membership to establish branches abroad, put down roots, and open up new territory.","The significance was entirely different.","“The first overseas branches will initially be established in three locations.”","“Amsterdam, in Helan, to cover the Western Continent market.”","“Singapore, to cover the Eastern Continent market.”","“And Silicon Valley in North America, to cover the North American market.”","“I need to select the first group of overseas core personnel from among you. There is only one requirement: you must understand local laws and be proficient in a foreign language.”","The announcement triggered another round of discussion below the stage.","“I’m not worried about the legal stuff, but the foreign language... I’ve failed the English proficiency test three times.”","“Amsterdam means they speak Dutch, right? How are we supposed to learn Helanese? Is there some kind of crash course?”","“I heard you can get by speaking Chinese in Singapore. Maybe I’ll sign up for Singapore first.”","“...”","Everyone was enthusiastic. Not a single person seemed reluctant to leave home, and no one regarded the assignment as exile. In fact, they all wanted to be the first pioneers to expand the organization’s territory overseas.","Listening to the brothers behind him argue animatedly, Ma Da could not resist picking up the microphone and joining in.","“Don’t panic, brothers! Miss Liu said this is only the first group. There’ll be a second and a third group later. If you start learning now, there’s still plenty of time. And if all else fails, I’ll personally open an English training course for you.”","“Brother Ma, have you even passed the English proficiency test yourself?” someone shouted from the audience.","Ma Da replied, “Who was that? Could you stop ruining the mood?”","The entire venue burst into laughter.","Vanderberg sat in the front row, barely managing to follow every word Liu Yutong said through his translation earpiece.","When the translation conveyed this part of the speech, the expression on Vanderberg’s face instantly became wonderfully complicated.","Helan? Amsterdam?","Helan was his homeland, and the headquarters of Southfly Capital was located in Amsterdam.","Miss Liu had chosen Helan as the first stop in her overseas expansion—and announced it right in front of him. Wasn’t she obviously sending him a message?","The meaning was simple: Don’t even think about going back on your word. The Wanlong Association’s people could go anywhere.","The more Vanderberg thought about it, the colder his back felt.","Was this young lady really that ruthless? Was she deliberately sending people to keep an eye on him because she was afraid he might cause trouble after returning home?","And the Wanlong Association was impressive in its own way. The world was so vast—how did it feel as though they wanted to control every corner of it?","Pony Ma, sitting beside him, turned his head and glanced at him. There was even more sympathy in his eyes than before.","He felt the same way. He also believed Miss Liu did not trust this fellow to return home without causing trouble, which was why she had sent people there.","How ruthless!",".........","Over the next three days, the Dragon Nation’s capital market was thrown into another frenzy.","The Wanlong Association Group, Wanlong Capital, Yunshan Capital, and Xuanhuang Capital—the global investment firm established later—joined forces to acquire a twenty-five-percent stake in Big Goose Group from Southfly Capital.","Combined with the five percent stake Liu Yutong had quietly accumulated over a long period through the secondary market, the total shareholding under her control had reached thirty percent. She had officially become Big Goose Group’s largest shareholder.","The news sent shock waves through the entire Dragon Nation business community.","After all, Big Goose was a colossal company with a market value of more than a hundred billion yuan. Yet without making a sound, its largest shareholder had changed hands.","The acquisition was discussed not only in financial circles, but also among the scions of the capital’s powerful families. They could not help marveling at it.","Liu Yutong was far too formidable.","She had swallowed Big Goose in one bite.","Naturally, quite a few of them were pleased to see the acquisition go through. Some had joined the Yunshan Circle, while others had joined the Xuanhuang Circle, and all of them stood to benefit from it.","Whether it was the Yunshan Circle or the Xuanhuang Circle, both were built on the same fundamental principle: binding people together through mutual interests.","Without the ties created by shared interests, why would anyone remain so loyal to you based on face and personal favors alone?","The difference was merely one of focus.","The Yunshan Circle targeted domestic connections, resources, and industries, while the Xuanhuang Circle leaned more toward international networks and capital.","The acquisition also sparked heated discussion among netizens and stock investors.","“Holy crap! The Wanlong Association really bought Big Goose?!”","“They didn’t buy the whole company. They just became its largest shareholder. But the meaning is basically the same. From today onward, Pony Ma has someone above him—and she’s a woman twenty years younger than him.”","“First they pinned Fruit Phones to the ground, and now they’ve swallowed Big Goose. What kind of monster is this company? Why hasn’t it gone public yet? I really want to buy their stock!”","“Wake up. If the Wanlong Association really wanted to go public, it would have done so ages ago. They don’t need your pocket change.”","“Hey, do you think Ma Yunyun is already packing his bags and preparing to run? His payment platform just got hammered by Longpay, and now Big Goose has been taken over by the Wanlong Association. Could Ali be next?”","“Ma Yunyun: How terrifying! These giant companies are gobbled up and acquired just like that. I’ve never been this nervous in my life.”","“Hahahaha... I’m dying. Old Ma might really be trembling in fear. After all, the Wanlong Association doesn’t play by any rules when it decides to deal with someone.”","“.........”","On the second trading day after the announcement, Big Goose Group and the Wanlong Association jointly held a press conference, officially announcing news that sent shock waves throughout the entire internet industry.","WeTalk and GooseChat have merged, and the unified brand following the merger will be WeTalk. All of GooseChat’s user data, technical teams, and operational resources will be incorporated into the WeTalk ecosystem.","WeTalk will also become part of Big Goose Group.","The moment the news broke, the Hong Kong stock market exploded.","Big Goose Group’s stock opened sharply higher that day, surging more than 40 percent from the previous session’s close.","Over the next several trading days, the stock continued to climb. From the depths it had sunk to before the announcement, it was dragged all the way back above HK$230, pushing the company’s market capitalization over the HK$300 billion mark once again—and the momentum was still incredibly strong.","Pony Ma stared at the data on the backend, cigarette in hand, unsure whether he should be happy or sigh.","The good news was that Big Goose’s stock had finally rebounded—and far more dramatically than expected.","The frustrating part was that this rebound had absolutely nothing to do with him personally. It was entirely the masterpiece of the newly crowned largest shareholder.","First, they had showered WeTalk users with a billion yuan in red packets, sending the platform’s user count through the roof. Then, while Big Goose’s stock was being trampled into the ground by the market, they had swooped in and bought the dip with pinpoint accuracy. Finally, they had used WeTalk—their trump card—to haul Big Goose’s market value back to the altar.","Every move had been tightly connected, flawless from beginning to end.","Even Pony Ma himself had become just another piece on the chessboard, arranged exactly where he was needed.","Financial media outlets collectively went into a frenzy.","“Big ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​‌‍Goose Stages a Comeback Against All Odds—Wanlong Emerges as the Biggest Winner.”","“From HK$400 Billion to Half That, Then a Violent Rebound—What Happened to Big Goose?”","“Snake Swallowing an Elephant or a Marriage of Equals? The Capital Logic Behind WeTalk’s Takeover of Big Goose”...","Headlines flooded the internet, with countless influencers practically itching to publish eight analysis articles a day.","Netizens who enjoyed browsing the finance forums also launched into heated discussions.","“I was wondering yesterday whether Big Goose was about to go bankrupt. Then I opened my stock app today and was completely dumbfounded. Is this a roller coaster?”","“At least roller coasters have safety restraints. Big Goose just launched straight into the sky.”","“I have a friend who works at Big Goose. Last year, he got a huge pile of stock options and was trapped with them for months. He was practically on the verge of a breakdown. This morning, after seeing the stock price, he posted more than a dozen updates on WeTalk Moments, and every single one just said, ‘Aaaaaah!’ I think he’s finally recovered.”","“You’re only looking at the stock price. I’m focused on something else. Based on the current market value, Wanlong has already made several tens of billions in unrealized gains on its acquisition of Nanfei Holdings. Several tens of billions! Not only did the acquisition cost them nothing—they actually made a fortune from it. Does that really make sense?”","“You think there’s something fishy going on?”","“It certainly looks suspicious. I’m now seriously wondering whether someone was secretly shorting Big Goose in the first place, which is why its stock price fell so disastrously.”","“Could this guy have been directing and acting in the whole show from start to finish?”","“Hey, you upstairs, watch what you say. Wanlong’s legal department is issuing a warning—another warning—and yet another warning!”","“My bad!”","“..........”"]},{"number":909,"title":"Chapter 909: 910. Xu Yangeng requests an audience.","paragraphs":["The shockwaves from Big Goose Group’s earth-shaking acquisition had finally subsided, and its stock price was continuing to soar.","That afternoon, Yu Xin arrived at Liu Yutong’s office carrying a stack of documents.","“Sister ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‍Yutong, the latest figures for the Alliance of Domestic Excellence are out. It’s been half a year since the alliance was established.”","“The alliance now has more than twenty members. After the supply chain was fully integrated, members’ procurement costs dropped by an average of 18 percent. Shipments of Loongson chips tripled compared with the previous quarter.”","Liu Yutong took the documents and flipped through them, nodding. “That’s good.”","“What about market share?”","“In the first quarter of this year, domestic smartphones broke through the 60 percent mark in the Chinese market!”","Sixty percent.","Liu Yutong raised her eyebrows slightly.","That figure had been reached at least a year earlier than in her previous life.","It seemed that the Alliance of Domestic Excellence had indeed created a catfish effect. Once the domestic manufacturers banded together, all the smaller companies that had originally been waiting on the sidelines rushed in as well, accelerating the entire market.","Most importantly, with alliance orders supporting it, Loongson’s shipments were growing steadily. Only with enough orders could the research team have the motivation and resources to push toward more advanced manufacturing processes.","That was what she valued most.","“You’ve done very well, but you need to work even harder. I’m still waiting for you to take over from me someday,” Liu Yutong said with a smile.","Yu Xin nodded. “I’ll do my best, Sister Yutong.”","“Oh, right, Sister Yutong. I’ve noticed some unusual signals in the market recently.”","“What kind of signals?”","“A few foreign brands have started making trouble in the supply chain.”","“Samsung suddenly raised the price of AMOLED screens and has been delaying production slots for our alliance members. A few smaller manufacturers have had their orders pushed back by as much as three months. And Qualcomm let it be known a few days ago that the licensing fees for its next-generation Snapdragon chips would be going up—by at least 10 percent.”","A cold glint flashed through Liu Yutong’s eyes.","“That’s the only trick these people know.”","“They may be feeling threatened. Our domestic smartphone brands have captured 60 percent of the market in just half a year. That’s far too fast—they probably never expected it. Samsung, Qualcomm, and the others are used to holding the supply chain hostage and collecting protection money. Now that they’ve suddenly realized they can’t control us anymore, they’re bound to panic.”","“I expect their next moves will only grow more ruthless. We can’t rule out the possibility that they’ll use their supply-chain advantages to divide and weaken our alliance.”","“What you’re saying—”","Liu Yutong was about to continue when the internal phone on her desk suddenly rang, interrupting her.","She pressed the speaker button, and Lan Die’s voice came through the speaker.","“The Young Lady, Professor Xu Yangen is here. He says he has something urgent to discuss with you.”","Liu Yutong was slightly surprised.","Xu Yangeng.","This professor from BS University had been rescued from a tenement building in Jinchuan the previous year. After receiving eight million yuan in start-up funding, he had moved straight into the laboratory and had barely shown his face in public for the past six months.","That was understandable. He was a research fanatic who disliked socializing.","But why had he suddenly come to see her today?","“Let him in.”","A moment later, Xu Yangeng pushed open the door and walked in.","Compared with last year, Professor Xu looked much healthier and more energetic.","However, his expression was somewhat off. He looked nervous and guilty.","“Director Liu, Mr. Yu,” Xu Yangeng said awkwardly.","Even now, whenever he thought about the young woman who had once eaten with his daughter in the cafeteria at BS University—and who had turned out to be the head of the Wanlonghui Group—he still felt as though he were in a daze.","A girl barely in her twenties was in charge of hundreds of thousands of people.","It was terrifying.","“Professor Xu, have a seat.” Liu Yutong pointed to the chair opposite her. “What brings you here?”","Xu Yangeng did not sit down. Instead, he pulled a stack of documents from his briefcase and handed them to Liu Yutong with both hands.","“Director Liu, I’m here to apply for additional funding.”","“For additional funding, you should speak with the relevant department.”","Although she said that, Liu Yutong took the documents and began flipping through them. Before long, her brows drew together slightly.","“Professor Xu, I gave you eight million yuan last year, and it hasn’t even been a full year. You’re already telling me it wasn’t enough?”","“Uh... it really wasn’t enough.”","“The equipment costs exceeded our expectations. I imported two high-precision battery cycle testers, and those two alone cost more than four million yuan. Some key experimental materials were also several dozen percent more expensive than anticipated,” Xu Yangeng explained.","“What else?” Liu Yutong continued flipping through the documents.","“We also conducted some exploratory research into the modification of cathode materials. You know how basic research is, Director Liu. It requires heavy investment in the early stages, takes a long time, and produces results slowly. It can’t be accomplished overnight. You have to keep experimenting, keep making mistakes, and keep burning money...”","The more he spoke, the guiltier he sounded, until his voice gradually grew quieter.","Liu Yutong did not respond. When she reached the final few pages, she suddenly looked up at Xu Yangeng.","“Professor Xu, you’re researching batteries, but I want you to tell me where exactly you’ve spent your time over the past six months.”","The question made Xu Yangeng stiffen all over. Panic was plainly visible on his face.","“I... I’ve obviously been researching batteries.”","“Have you?”","Liu Yutong turned to a particular page and pointed at the rows of experimental data.","“Doping and modification experiments on the cathode materials of lithium iron phosphate batteries. Research into the thermal stability of high-nickel cathode materials for ternary lithium batteries. Solutions for suppressing the shuttle effect in lithium-sulfur batteries. Optimization of ionic conductivity in solid-state electrolytes...”","“Professor Xu, you’ve been working on so many different areas over the past six months. But after looking through all these pages, why is there so little on optimizing the charging and discharging performance of smartphone lithium batteries?”","Sweat began to bead on Xu Yangeng’s forehead.","“Director Liu, please let me explain. These lines of research are actually interconnected. As long as we achieve a breakthrough in the core materials, improving smartphone battery performance will follow naturally. Essentially, it’s a process of transferring the technology...”","“Professor Xu.”","There was a trace of helplessness in Liu Yutong’s voice.","“I gave you eight million yuan to develop smartphone batteries first. I’m not saying that the research you’re doing isn’t important, but it belongs to an entirely different field—the new-energy vehicle battery sector, not the smartphone batteries we urgently need right now.”","“I know what you want to do, and I understand your passion. But business is business. Every investment needs to generate returns. You can’t take my money, focus only on the research you’re interested in, then come back and tell me the money isn’t enough and ask for more. That isn’t appropriate, is it?”","Xu Yangeng was left speechless.","Seeing his expression, Liu Yutong sighed softly.","She understood people like Xu Yangeng all too well.","He was a pure technician, with his head full of technological ideals and a passion for research. He simply couldn’t control himself.","Asking someone like him to calmly focus on developing a single product was indeed asking a lot.","She would have to think of a way to put some restraints on him.","Just then, the office door suddenly flew open.","Lan Die hurried in and leaned over to whisper a few words into Liu Yutong’s ear.","Liu Yutong’s expression changed instantly.","“When did this happen?”","“Half an hour ago. It’s already blown up online.”"]},{"number":910,"title":"Chapter 910: 911, mobile phone explosions, external enemies.","paragraphs":["The Longyao S1 had exploded.","When Liu Yutong and Yu Xin heard the news, their expressions changed immediately.","Liu Yutong had Lan Die pull up the photos posted on online forums.","In the pictures, the remains of a Longyao S1 had been laid out on a white tabletop. A fist-sized hole had been burned straight through the center of the screen, while charred marks spread from the middle of the phone to the entire rear half of the device like some disgusting vine.","The black casing had been completely warped by the intense heat. Its edges had curled upward, exposing the scorched components inside. The sight was horrifying.","A charging cable lay beside the phone. Its connector was burned black as well, with the wires melted into a single lump.","The accompanying caption consisted of only a few short lines, but it had already caused an uproar.","[Longyao S1 suddenly explodes while charging, burns through a nightstand, and nearly sets the entire bedroom on fire! So this is the so-called pride of domestic manufacturing?]","The comments section had already gone wild.","“Holy crap! The battery exploded? Is this for real?”","“I used to praise the Longyao S1 for its great value, but this scares me so badly I’m not sure I dare use the one I have.”","“No way! I just ordered a Longyao S1. Can I return it now? Urgent, urgent, urgent!”","“Longyao is in serious trouble this time. A battery explosion is no joke. Someone could actually get killed. If Longyao mishandles this, they could be finished.”","“I suggest that all Longyao S1 users stop using their phones immediately. Whatever you do, don’t charge them overnight. Your life is more important.”","“Is the Wanlonghui Group going to give us an explanation, or are they planning to pretend nothing happened?”","“Don’t rush to judgment. It’s only been half an hour. They might already be holding a meeting. But seriously, a battery-related safety incident is far more serious than some plagiarism accusation about the phone’s appearance. If Longyao doesn’t handle this properly, they could be done for.”","“...”","The discussion in the comments continued to intensify, showing no sign of dying down.","After briefly scrolling through several pages, Liu Yutong asked, “Lan Die, what’s the situation now?”","“It’s very bad. The public backlash is spreading rapidly. Aside from Weibo, which we can control, people are discussing this on Tieba, Tianya, and all the major tech forums. We’ve also noticed that many accounts are posting highly coordinated messages, using very professional wording. They don’t look like ordinary users speaking spontaneously. It’s more likely that organized online trolls are fanning the flames.”","“Have you traced the source?”","“The technical team is investigating, but we haven’t located it yet. The other side is very careful. They’re using a distributed posting strategy, with large numbers of accounts publishing similar content at the same time. Their IP addresses are scattered across the country, and some are using proxies. It’s very difficult to trace them back to the real source.”","Liu Yutong nodded. She reopened the photo of the exploded battery, enlarged it, and studied it carefully for a long time.","The phone carcass in the photo was indeed a Longyao S1. At the very least, the casing and logo matched.","“Yu Xin, have the factory send over the quality-inspection records for every battery batch, especially those from the past three months.","“Also, immediately suspend all online and offline sales of the affected battery. Notify every distributor and store that customers who have already purchased a Longyao S1 and are concerned about their safety may replace the battery free of charge. The group will cover the cost.”","She continued, “And have Zhao Tianyi prepare an official statement. The wording must be sincere but not weak. There are two key points: first, we take this incident extremely seriously and have launched a comprehensive investigation. Second, until the investigation is complete, all sales and shipments of the Longyao S1 will be suspended.”","“Yes, Sister Tong!” Yu Xin replied.","“The Young Lady, there’s one more thing. The supply-chain department just sent word that the battery involved in this Longyao phone explosion appears to have been imported. Most of the imported batteries were manufactured under contract by Two-Star,” Lan Die reported again.","Liu Yutong’s eyes narrowed slightly.","“Two-Star?”","“Yes.”","Yu Xin suddenly remembered something as well. “Our battery supply is divided into two channels. One comes from domestic contract manufacturers, but their production capacity is very limited. The other consists of imported batteries. Among those suppliers, Two-Star accounts for the largest share—more than sixty percent.”","Liu Yutong suddenly recalled the Two-Star phone explosions from her previous life. Those incidents would not be exposed for several more years, yet now they had appeared prematurely in Longyao phones.","“How interesting.” She smiled faintly.","Then she turned to Professor Xu. “Professor Xu, aren’t you fond of conducting research? Here’s your chance. If you can find out the root cause of this explosion, I won’t just give you the additional investment you requested—I’ll double it.","“But if you can’t figure it out...”","She paused before continuing, “Then consider your previous investment a mistake on my part.”","Professor Xu’s expression became extremely serious.","He naturally understood what Liu Yutong meant.","She wasn’t joking, nor was she trying to intimidate him. She was giving him one final opportunity to prove his worth.","He had already witnessed the way The Young Lady did things. Once she made a decision, she never went back on it.","“Director Liu, I promise I’ll find out the truth.”","“Give me three days—just three days. I’ll give you a satisfactory answer.”","“Fine. Three days.”","Without ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌​‍another word, Professor Xu grabbed the documents from the desk and hurried out.","Watching him leave, Yu Xin couldn’t help shaking her head. “Sister Yutong, you scared him.”","“If I didn’t scare him, he wouldn’t know what he was supposed to do.” Liu Yutong turned to Lan Die. “Find those online trolls. No matter who’s behind them, make them pay the price!”","“Yes, The Young Lady!”","“Oh, right, The Young Lady. There’s one more thing I nearly forgot to mention.”","“What is it?”","“Three days ago, there was another incident overseas involving an exploding battery in a certain Two-Star phone model. It happened in Florida in the United States. A user accidentally left the phone in a car, and it ended up setting the vehicle on fire. Fortunately, no one was injured.”","“The news sparked a small wave of discussion in overseas tech circles. Some people in China’s tech community noticed it as well, but public attention is now focused entirely on our Longyao phone. They seem to be deliberately avoiding any mention of who manufactured the battery and are intentionally directing all the blame toward us.”","After hearing this, Liu Yutong quietly uttered eight words:","“Replacing the flowers, borrowing the knife to kill.”","“Exactly.” Lan Die nodded.","Liu Yutong said, “It seems this isn’t an ordinary public-relations battle. Someone is using public opinion as a weapon to make a major move.”","Yu Xin’s expression changed. “Sister Yutong, you mean...”","Liu Yutong nodded. “They’re probably not from our country.”","Fruit, Two-Star, Qualcomm... Every one of these international giants had ample motive.","The establishment of the Domestic Products Alliance would certainly mean strong support for local supply chains, which would threaten them. Perhaps the threat was not significant for the time being, but who would willingly sit back and watch you rise?","“Whether this was done by one company or several of them working together, they have only one goal: to make consumers lose faith in domestic brands and bring down the Domestic Products Alliance.”","“If that’s the case, then I’m afraid we’ll be facing more than just a public-opinion backlash. Small disruptions in the supply chain, exclusion from distribution channels, and even pressure at the policy level could all follow one after another.” By the time Yu Xin finished speaking, she too felt the immense pressure bearing down on them.","“Then let them come.” Liu Yutong was utterly undaunted. “That day was bound to come sooner or later. It just so happens that Wanlong will be the first to bear the brunt. Before that happens, though, let’s teach them a good lesson. For starters, let’s force Erxing out of the domestic market.”"]},{"number":911,"title":"Chapter 911: 912, Battery Defect.","paragraphs":["Two days later, in the capital of BS Province.","In the Northern High-Tech Development Zone stood a gray-and-white three-story building housing an advanced energy materials laboratory.","Sister Yutong had funded the laboratory the previous year. Although it could not compare with the large overseas facilities that routinely cost tens of millions of dollars, it was just about sufficient for Xu Yangeng to conduct his research.","When Yu Xin arrived, the laboratory doors were wide open, and heated arguments could be heard from inside.","She did not enter immediately. Instead, she stood quietly at the doorway and listened.","She had asked to come here herself. Until the battery issue was fully investigated, she would not be able to put her mind at ease.","Longyao S1 was the first major project she had followed from beginning to end since joining the Wanlong Association. The success or failure of this product would directly determine her standing and influence within the group.","Sister Yutong had already made things clear to her: Longyao had to break into the global top five within two years. If she succeeded, the position of CEO of the Wanlong Association Group would be hers.","In truth, Yu Xin understood that this condition had been set for everyone else to see. For a young woman to take that position, Sister Yutong’s trust alone was not enough. She had to produce tangible results and silence all opposition.","Now that Longyao was facing such a serious crisis, she had to personally oversee the situation before she could feel at ease.","When ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​‍Yu Xin entered the laboratory, Professor Xu was standing in front of a workbench, holding a dismantled battery that had been burned black. A bloody gash ran across his face, and blood was still oozing from the wound, yet he seemed completely unaware of it.","Behind him, several bespectacled researchers were arguing heatedly over the direction of their research. Their faces were flushed with anger.","“I’ve told you countless times! The doping ratio of the cathode material has to be increased by another two percentage points! Your proposal simply won’t work!”","“Two percentage points? Easy for you to say! What happens to lattice stability after the doping ratio is increased? If the structure collapses, you won’t be able to make anything at all. Who are you going to answer to then?”","“Stability can be optimized later. The most important thing right now is to get the entire process running. If you can’t even get the process to work, what’s the point of talking about stability?”","“You’re putting the cart before the horse!”","“You’re the one doing nothing but talking theory!”","“...”","Yu Xin stood at the doorway and listened for a few moments. She more or less understood what these professors and experts were arguing about.","Without saying anything, she first looked around the laboratory, taking everything in.","The raw-material mixer, coating machine, agitator, roller press, electrode-sheet cutter... The equipment was fairly complete.","The whiteboard on the wall beside the window was densely covered with experimental data.","Even from those records alone, it was clear that Professor Xu had put tremendous effort into his research.","Although he became tongue-tied whenever he spoke with her or Sister Yutong, he was a completely different person in the laboratory—meticulous, serious, and almost fanatical.","That was probably what Sister Yutong had seen in him when she decided to invest in his work.","“Professor Xu,” Yu Xin called out.","Professor Xu abruptly raised his head. When he saw Yu Xin standing at the doorway, he froze for a moment, then instinctively wiped the blood from his face with the back of his hand. Instead, he smeared the blood everywhere, making himself look even more disheveled.","“President... President Yu, what brings you here personally?”","“I wanted to come and take a look. I won’t feel at ease unless I oversee this myself.” Yu Xin walked up to him and pointed at his face. “What happened to you?”","“It’s nothing, nothing. I was doing a thermal runaway test just now and got splashed by accident. It’s only a superficial wound.” Professor Xu dismissed it casually.","Then he immediately held out the charred battery in his hand and said, “President Yu, you came at just the right time. Take a look at this.”","Yu Xin accepted the battery remains.","Its casing had been badly warped by the intense heat. The metal foil along the edges had curled outward, exposing the anode material, which had been burned through and turned a charred black. A pungent chemical odor hung in the air.","“I just conducted a thermal stability test at fifty degrees Celsius.”","“Do you know what happened? The battery began to swell at fifty degrees. At fifty-five degrees, the internal separator shrank, causing the positive and negative electrodes to short-circuit directly. It exploded in less than three seconds.”","“It exploded at fifty degrees?” Yu Xin’s expression darkened.","“Yes! Fifty degrees!”","“A normal lithium-ion phone battery has a thermal runaway threshold of at least 130 degrees Celsius. Better ones can reach 150 or even 180 degrees. But this battery exploded at fifty degrees. Do you understand what that means? In summer, if you leave your phone in a car, the interior temperature can easily exceed sixty degrees after two hours in the sun. At that point, the phone is no longer a phone—it’s a time bomb in your pocket.”","Yu Xin asked, “So this isn’t an isolated quality-control issue. The battery itself has a major design flaw?”","“Exactly.” Professor Xu nodded. He turned around, picked up a freshly printed inspection report from the workbench, and flipped through it until he reached a particular page. “After dismantling the battery, I discovered that, in order to make the phone thinner, they compressed the separator between the positive and negative electrodes to its absolute limit.”","“Look at this figure. A normal separator should be between twenty and twenty-five micrometers thick. This battery’s separator is only twelve micrometers—nearly half as thick. The material is also problematic. The standard material should be a ceramic-coated separator, which has good thermal stability and does not shrink easily at high temperatures. Its only drawback is that it costs more.”","“But this battery uses the cheapest polyolefin separator. It shrinks extremely quickly at high temperatures. Once it shrinks, it breaks, and once it breaks, the positive and negative electrodes come into direct contact. Of course it exploded.”","“The electrolyte formula is also seriously flawed.”","“I analyzed its composition and found that the electrolyte contains a large amount of low-boiling-point solvent. The purpose is to improve discharge efficiency at room temperature and make the benchmark results look better. But the price is that the low-boiling-point solvent vaporizes rapidly at high temperatures, causing the pressure inside the battery to rise sharply.”","“With a separator as thin as paper, one side is the rapidly increasing internal pressure, while the other is the separator shrinking and rupturing under heat. The two forces act together, and the battery explodes.”","“So this isn’t a technical problem at all. They deliberately sacrificed safety to cut costs and make the performance figures look good.”","“This is corner-cutting! They’re treating human lives as if they mean nothing!”","“Whoever made this battery completely disregarded the users’ safety. They have no moral bottom line whatsoever!” Professor Xu cursed furiously.","After listening to him, Yu Xin had already formed her own judgment. This probably had not been done to cut costs through inferior materials.","To be honest, for a company of Erxing’s caliber, that bit of money was nothing. There was no reason to risk the credibility of its entire supply chain.","A more reasonable explanation was that the other side had deliberately done this to make Longyao’s phones fail and deal Longyao a devastating blow.","Of course, she did not share this suspicion with them. She planned to tell Sister Yutong later.","Besides, such a serious failure in the battery supply chain was also her responsibility. After all, she had failed to detect it in advance.","Yu Xin suppressed the thoughts rising in her mind, pulled a tissue from her pocket, and held it out to him. She pointed at Xu Yangeng’s face. “Wipe the blood off first.”","Xu Yangeng froze for a moment before belatedly realizing that his face was throbbing with pain. He quickly took the tissue and pressed it against the wound, giving an awkward smile. “Thank you, President Yu.”","Yu Xin said nothing more. She picked up the test report and read through it carefully from beginning to end.","Every figure in the report was supported by detailed test records. From the separator’s thickness and the analysis of the electrolyte’s composition to the critical temperature for thermal runaway and the expansion curve after an internal short circuit, every detail was laid out clearly and precisely.","Even though she wasn’t an expert in batteries, she could immediately tell where the problem with this battery lay.","At last, she closed the report and looked at Xu Yangeng again.","“Professor Xu, can you confirm it one more time? Use the batteries supplied by Erxing and conduct another complete round of thermal stability tests. Record the entire process and all the results. I need evidence that everyone can understand—evidence no one can refute.”","Xu Yangeng nodded. “No problem! I’ll start right away! Who was it? Little Li, go to the warehouse and bring out all the battery samples supplied by Erxing. Take ten samples from every batch, from the first shipment to the latest one, and run a complete thermal stability test on all of them.”","“Everyone else, come over and lend a hand. We’re working overtime tonight. Organize all the test data into a formal report. The format must be standardized, and every cited standard must be clearly listed. Not a single punctuation mark can be wrong.”","“Also, seal and preserve the remains of the battery that exploded just now. Take photographs for the record. Number and archive every fragment...”","As he spoke, he rolled up his sleeves and prepared to get to work. The awkwardness he had shown in front of Yu Xin was gone completely, replaced by an excited, focused expression.","The researcher known as Little Li hesitated before offering a quiet reminder. “Professor Xu, shouldn’t you have your face treated first? The wound looks fairly deep. What if it gets infected...”","“It’s just a minor flesh wound. It won’t kill me! Hurry up and run the tests!”","“But...”","“No buts. Go!”","Little Li nodded, grabbed the notebook, and hurried off toward the warehouse.","Xu Yangeng put on his safety goggles and gloves and personally began assembling a new testing apparatus.","Watching his almost self-forgetting figure as he worked, Yu Xin felt something stir inside her.","Suddenly, she said, “Professor Xu.”","“Hmm?”","“As long as you can identify the root cause of this explosion and complete the battery redesign on the existing foundation, raising its safety performance above industry standards, I’ll help secure more funding for you. From now on, I also won’t restrict the direction of your research.”","Xu Yangeng froze. He turned to look at Yu Xin, never expecting her to make such a weighty promise.","But once he recovered, he nodded excitedly. “Thank you, President Yu. I’ll give it everything I’ve got and develop a better battery.”","What Xu Yangeng didn’t know was that this matter was extremely important not only to him, but to Yu Xin as well.","She couldn’t let the Longyao project collapse under a wave of public attacks. Nor could she allow herself to fail; otherwise, she would have no face to take over as CEO of the Wanlonghui Group.","“For the next few days, I’ll stay here and work alongside all of you.”","“Let’s solve this problem once and for all!”","“Together.”"]},{"number":912,"title":"Chapter 912: 913, Battery modification completed.","paragraphs":["Online public opinion had grown increasingly fierce by the third day after the Longyao S1 explosion was exposed.","At first, the discussion had been limited to a small circle of tech enthusiasts. But as more and more “victims” stepped forward and spoke out, while media outlets rushed to repost the story, the incident quickly broke out of that circle and landed on the front pages of all the major portals.","“Longyao Phone Explodes While Charging, User Narrowly Escapes Death After Being Woken in the Middle of the Night!”","“Beacon of Domestic Industry or a Ticking Time Bomb? Questions Raised Over the Longyao S1’s Safety!”","“Wanlonghui Group Remains Silent—Where Are Consumers’ Rights?”","The headlines grew more sensational by the hour, and the atmosphere of panic intensified along with them.","In truth, it would not have been difficult for Wanlonghui to suppress the negative coverage. This was not the later era, when information spread through countless channels. Apart from the official media, the main avenues for news distribution were Weibo and a handful of major portal sites.","But neither Liu Yutong nor Yu Xin chose to intervene. They allowed public opinion to continue fermenting.","Because they intended to settle this account with the people pulling the strings behind the scenes.","On Weibo, an account claiming to belong to a “victim of the Longyao S1 explosion” posted a lengthy article accompanied by several shocking photographs: a charred bedside table, soot-blackened walls, and the mangled remains of a phone that had been blown apart.","The post described the terrifying incident in detail. The phone had been charging beside the bed when, at three in the morning, it suddenly began making a sizzling noise. A moment later, flames flashed violently, and the phone exploded, nearly burning the user to death.","Within two hours of being posted, the Weibo entry had been reposted more than a hundred thousand times, while the number of comments continued to soar.","“That’s terrifying! I had my Longyao S1 charging beside my bed too. After reading this, I threw it straight into the living room.”","“My wife just found out she’s pregnant, and we use Longyao phones at home. She’s so anxious she can’t sleep. Wanlonghui, come out and give us an explanation!”","“I used to think Longyao offered great value for money. Now it looks like you really do get what you pay for. They even cut corners on the battery—aren’t they treating consumers’ lives like a joke?”","“My cousin works at a phone repair shop. He says they’ve been seeing a lot more Longyao S1s lately, and many of them have swollen batteries. They just haven’t exploded yet.”","“Beacon of domestic industry? What a joke! Trash company!”","“.........”","Every now and then, a few rational voices appeared, urging everyone to wait for the results of the official investigation. But they were quickly drowned out by the overwhelming wave of condemnation.","“Wait for the investigation? Samsung batteries have exploded too, so why don’t you people get this worked up about that? Hypocrites!”","“Exactly. The Longyao uses batteries made by Samsung. Why aren’t you attacking Samsung?”","The moment those two comments appeared, a mob descended on them.","“Shills are here! Wanlonghui is starting its damage control!”","“Samsung’s phones exploded under its own brand. The Longyao exploded with Longyao’s logo on it. How can those be the same? If a component you purchased is defective, shouldn’t you bear the primary responsibility?”","“If you find a fly in your food at a restaurant, do you curse the restaurant or the farmer who grew the ingredients? If you can’t even come up with a decent analogy, stop embarrassing yourself.”","“Where’s the proof that Samsung batteries exploded? One screenshot from some foreign news report? Who knows whether Wanlonghui made it up to shift the blame!”","“Longyao shills are disgusting!”","“.........”","The war spread from Weibo to Tieba, then from Tieba to all the major tech forums.","In every post discussing Longyao’s batteries, someone repeatedly emphasized the same point: the Longyao S1 used batteries manufactured by Samsung. Samsung was the source of the problem; Longyao had merely been dragged into it.","But those voices were suppressed so thoroughly that they could never gain traction.","Someone was clearly controlling public opinion in a highly organized manner, crushing every rational argument before it could rise to the surface.","For a time, the words “Longyao phones” became synonymous with public disgrace. Whoever mentioned them was attacked.","Even the other brands in the Beacon of Domestic Industry Alliance were dragged into the fallout. Dami, Lianxiang... nearly every domestic phone manufacturer was hauled out and publicly torn apart one by one.","“Beacon of Domestic Industry Alliance? I’d call it the Alliance of Domestic Shame!”","“Domestic phones are just piles of cheap components thrown together. Their safety standards are a complete mess. You’re better off spending a little extra on an Apple.”","“At least Apple phones don’t explode.”","“.........”","BS Province. The laboratory.","Yu Xin had spent the past few days in the lab, keeping a close eye on the battery research.","Of course, she also checked the online reaction on her laptop every day. She was furious each time, but forced herself to endure it without sending anyone in to intervene.","In addition, the group had sent her an investigation report.","The report showed that at least seven public-relations firms were working simultaneously to fuel the backlash surrounding the Longyao S1 explosions. More than twenty thousand paid accounts had been deployed, with posts appearing across virtually every Chinese-language internet platform in the country.","After tracing the funds used to hire those PR firms through layers of shell companies and affiliated entities, investigators had ultimately determined that the money originated overseas.","There was no way to identify exactly who abroad was directing the operation, but it hardly mattered. None of those foreign giants were innocent.","Apple included.","After reading the report, Yu Xin rubbed her temples.","To be honest, she had weathered her share of crises since entering the industry. But this was the first time she had ever faced a coordinated assault by multiple global giants.","It would have been a lie to say she wasn’t nervous.","But she also understood that the more dangerous the situation, the less room there was for panic.","Sister Yutong had handed this mess to her precisely to see whether she could hold the line.","If she endured, she would have earned her place as Wanlonghui’s CEO.","If she failed, then...","Yu Xin closed the laptop, stood up, and walked over to Xu Yangeng.","Xu Yangeng was leaning over the lab bench, his eyes fixed without blinking on the curves moving across the oscilloscope.","The wound on his left cheek—the one caused by flying debris three days earlier—had scabbed over, though it had not fully healed. It looked like an ugly centipede clinging to his skin.","“Professor Xu, how much longer?”","“Almost there.”","Xu Yangeng carefully lifted a tiny piece of separator peeled from the improved battery with a pair of tweezers. After examining it under the microscope for a while, he recorded several figures in his lab notebook.","“We adjusted the doping ratio of the cathode material by three percentage points, replaced the separator with one coated in ceramic, and increased its thickness from twelve microns to twenty-three. We also modified the electrolyte formula, reducing the proportion of low-boiling-point solvents to within the safe threshold. We ran comparative tests on six different designs, with ten samples in each group. The results are in.”","He handed her the notebook.","Yu ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‍Xin took it and read through the entries line by line.","“Constant-temperature test at 50°C—swelling rate: 0%.","“High-temperature impact test at 80°C—no obvious shrinkage of the separator.","“Hot-box test at 130°C—the battery casing expanded slightly, but there was no short circuit, fire, or explosion.","“Extreme test at 150°C—the separator began to show slight shrinkage, but remained intact. The positive and negative electrodes still did not come into direct contact.”","The ultimate destructive test at 200°C—the battery eventually caught fire, but the entire process lasted more than three minutes, and the flames shot out in a controlled stream rather than erupting in an instant.","What did this mean?","It meant that even if the battery really were exposed to extreme heat, the user would have enough time to deal with the potential danger, instead of being given no time at all to react, as had happened with that previous two-star battery, which exploded at just 50°C.","“Professor Xu, this is...”","“We did it.”","Xu Yangeng straightened up. After staying up and working for several days and nights in a row, his eyes were bloodshot, but his expression was filled with excitement.","“All the test data is here. I’m willing to stake my life on this: after our improvements, the battery’s thermal runaway threshold has risen from 50°C to above 150°C. Its safety has increased threefold.”","Yu Xin was instantly overjoyed.","They had done it.","They really had.","“Professor Xu, thank you for all your hard work.” Yu Xin gave him a solemn bow.","Xu Yangeng was startled by the gesture. “No, no, no, Mr. Yu, what are you doing? This is simply part of my job.”","Yu Xin looked at him seriously. “Professor Xu, I’ll report everything you’ve done these past few days to Sister Yutong truthfully. Don’t worry. I will absolutely keep my promise to you.”","Xu Yangeng froze for a moment, then broke into a wide grin. Wasn’t securing sufficient research funding one of the reasons he had worked himself to the bone?","“Thank you, Mr. Yu!”","Yu Xin took out her phone and dialed Liu Yutong’s number.","“Sister Yutong, Professor Xu has done it.”","It took two seconds before Liu Yutong’s calm voice came through the phone.","“Good. Leave the rest to me.”","Yu Xin ended the call and turned to look out the window.","A pale sliver of dawn appeared along the horizon.","A new day had begun.","And so had Longyao’s counterattack."]},{"number":913,"title":"Chapter 913: 914, Surround and Kill.","paragraphs":["Mingzhu City, Shunchang Tower.","Just as Liu Yutong set down the phone, Zhao Tianyi pushed open the door and walked in.","“Miss, as you instructed, everything overseas has been arranged.”","Zhao Tianyi adjusted his gold-rimmed glasses. “One of Samsung’s flagship models in the North American market uses the same batch of batteries as the Longyao S1. That model has sold roughly three million units in North America.”","“Where’s the report?”","“Right here.” Zhao Tianyi pulled a document from his briefcase and handed it over with both hands. “This report contains a detailed comparison between the batteries Samsung supplied to Longyao and the batteries they use in their own phones. The results are largely identical. Although the thermal runaway threshold is slightly higher in Samsung’s own batteries, they’re still dangerous. There’s room for us to work with.”","Liu Yutong accepted the report and flipped through several pages before nodding. “Tianyi, what do you think of Samsung’s move?”","Without hesitation, Zhao Tianyi gave his verdict. “Stupid. Incredibly stupid.”","“They probably thought our companies in Longguo were easy to bully. But they forgot one thing.”","“What’s that?”","“We’re the Wanlong Association.”","“The Wanlong Association never holds grudges either, because...” Liu Yutong’s lips curved into a faint smile. “When someone crosses us, we settle the score on the spot.”","“Translate Yu Xin’s report, along with the report obtained from the United States, into English. Attach all the original experimental data and video recordings, then send everything to the American consumer protection organizations, the Consumer Product Safety Commission, and every major overseas media outlet we can reach.”","“Also, contact the Xuanhuang Society’s members in North America and have them push for a class-action lawsuit in the United States. Samsung has sold three million phones there. Surely at least one in a thousand—or even one in a hundred—users will have an accident, right? With that many battery explosions, Samsung will have a lot to answer for.”","Zhao Tianyi immediately understood. “Understood. Jesse will arrange for people to purchase large numbers of Samsung phones. It’s unusually hot in North America right now, so phones left inside cars exploding will be perfectly normal.”","Liu Yutong said nothing. Some things were better left understood without being spoken aloud.","“Miss, there’s one more thing. We found another force secretly fanning the flames.”","“Who?”","“The Takahashi Consortium from Japan.”","Liu Yutong turned around, her brows lifting slightly as the name gradually stirred her memory.","The Takahashi Consortium?","She remembered it now.","Back when Yu Xin was in charge of the phone business, she had proposed importing an LCD panel production line from Japan. The Takahashi Consortium had obstructed the deal and deliberately sabotaged it, forcing the plan to fall through. Later, Liu Yutong had used a number of connections and gone through several intermediaries before finally obtaining the production line through other channels.","“Heh... I suppose this is what happens when you become too powerful and attract too much attention?”","“Miss, should we send the Takahashi Consortium a little return gift?” Zhao Tianyi asked.","“They blocked our LCD panel deal, and now they’re taking advantage of the situation. Settling the old and new accounts together wouldn’t be excessive, would it?”","“Not at all. It’s completely justified.” Zhao Tianyi adjusted his glasses, his smile growing even wider.","“Not yet. Meals have to be eaten one bite at a time, and accounts have to be settled one at a time. We’ll deal with Samsung first. Apple and the Takahashi Consortium can wait their turn.” As she spoke, Liu Yutong took out her phone and dialed an international number.","The call was answered after two rings.","“Jesse, have the Xuanhuang Society’s North American branch prepare to initiate a class-action lawsuit. I’ll have Zhao Tianyi send over the relevant evidence and documents.”","Jesse’s respectful voice came from the other end. “Great-grand-aunt, who’s the target?”","“Samsung Electronics.”","“Understood.”","After hanging up, Liu Yutong gave Zhao Tianyi another instruction. “Also, have Yuncheng make the arrangements. Starting today, all Wanlong supermarkets and Wanlong malls under our group’s commercial retail division are to stop purchasing every Samsung product. This isn’t just about the Longyao phone. Across every consumer-facing outlet operated by the Wanlong Association, all Samsung products are to be removed from the shelves.”","“Also notify President Ma in Hangzhou, Mr. Liu in the capital, and Suning’s Mr. Zhang. The e-commerce platforms are to blacklist Samsung as well.”","Zhao Tianyi said, “Miss, that’s a ruthless move.”","A significant portion of Samsung’s revenue in Longguo came from home appliances and consumer electronics. Although the retail channels under the Wanlong Association had not yet covered the entire country, their reach in BS Province and several provinces in eastern China was already formidable.","Moreover, Wanlong’s channels had one distinctive trait: consumers trusted them deeply.","Wanlong supermarkets had always insisted on carefully selecting quality products and had never sold counterfeit or substandard goods. As a result, they enjoyed an exceptionally strong reputation among consumers.","Now that the Wanlong Association had announced it was suspending sales of Samsung products, it did not need to say another word. Consumers would draw their own conclusions.","Why had Wanlong supermarkets stopped selling Samsung products?","Was there something wrong with Samsung?","Then, with President Ma, Mr. Liu, Mr. Zhang, and the other major retail and e-commerce channels all removing Samsung products, Samsung’s presence in the Longguo market was essentially finished.","Sure enough, the moment the Wanlong Association Group’s official account posted the announcement, public opinion exploded once again.","“After verification by the Group’s Supply Chain and Logistics Division, a certain batch of lithium batteries supplied by Samsung Electronics has been found to contain serious safety hazards. The battery separators are only half as thick as the industry standard, while the thermal runaway threshold is as low as 50°C, presenting a significant safety risk.”","“To protect consumer rights and interests, all retail channels under the Wanlong Association Group will suspend sales of all Samsung products effective immediately. The date of resumption will be announced separately.”","“Furthermore, because the Longyao S1 contains batteries purchased from Samsung that pose a serious safety hazard, our company has decided to issue full refunds for all 4.2 million Longyao S1 phones already sold. We also reserve the right to pursue Samsung Electronics for all resulting losses and damages through legal channels.”","Three announcements, each more explosive than the last.","After seeing the bombshell statements, the comment section erupted completely.","“Holy crap! A full refund? They’re refunding all 4.2 million units?”","“Did I read that right? The Longyao S1 sold for 2,999 yuan each. Four point two million units—that’s how much money in total? I’m terrible at math. Can someone calculate it?”","“2,999 multiplied by 4.2 million comes to... roughly 12.5 billion yuan.”","“They’re ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​‌‍really refunding 12.5 billion just like that?”","“Longyao is incredible!”","“...”","After the Wanlong Association released the relevant testing videos and announced its follow-up measures, Alibaba, JD.com, Suning, and other companies successively issued statements announcing the complete removal of Samsung products, citing consumer safety concerns.","After that, other domestic retailers followed suit as well.","This was no longer merely a business rivalry.","It was an all-out encirclement.","It also demonstrated the terrifying power of the Wanlong Association Group."]},{"number":914,"title":"Chapter 914: 915. Hit a steel plate.","paragraphs":["Public opinion swung instantly after the Wanlong Association released the test evidence and announced a full-refund plan for the Longyao S1 battery explosion incident.","The flood of criticism that had originally dominated the internet turned overnight toward Twostar instead. Public opinion of Longyao also changed from outright condemnation to praise as a “conscientious company” and the “backbone of domestic brands.”","Twelve and a half billion yuan—refunded just like that.","Such a move seemed unprecedented in the history of global business.","Netizens even joked that this was the most expensive after-sales service in history. But, admittedly, the effect was immediate. At the very least, Longyao had shown real responsibility with real money instead of making empty promises.","“Twostar batteries explode at just fifty degrees Celsius. This isn’t a technical problem—it’s attempted murder for profit!”","“I looked into it. Twostar uses battery separators that are eighteen microns thick in its own products, but the ones it sold to Longyao were only twelve microns. The double standard is way too obvious. So the lives of consumers in the Long Kingdom don’t matter?”","“Boycott Twostar! I’m starting now!”","“Don’t just talk about it—do something. I’ve already sold the Twostar TV at home as scrap. I’m switching to a domestic brand right away.”","“Wanlong Supermarket has removed every Twostar product from its shelves. Ali and Dongdong have followed suit. This is a genuine nationwide ban. As far as the Long Kingdom market is concerned, Twostar can pretty much start digging its own grave.”","“I have to admit, I’m impressed by Longyao’s move. Twelve and a half billion yuan, refunded just like that. This isn’t merely cutting off an arm to survive. This is chopping off the entire arm to prove its innocence.”","Amid ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‍the wave of praise, a few skeptical voices naturally emerged.","“Could the Wanlong Association be making such a huge spectacle just to whitewash itself?”","The comment had barely been posted when people immediately tore into it.","“Whitewash itself? You think it would throw twelve and a half billion yuan in cash at the problem just to clear its name? Is the detergent in your house made of gold?”","“If you’re so capable, come up with twelve and a half billion yuan and try whitewashing yourself.”","“......”","That same day, the Consumer Rights Protection Association and the Consumer Product Safety Commission of the United States both received a complete evidence package submitted by operatives arranged by the North American branch of the Xuanhuang Society.","The package contained not only disassembly test data and complete video recordings of the Longyao S1 battery, but also an inspection report on a flagship Twostar phone sold in North America that used batteries from the same defective batch.","The report showed that although the battery separators in Twostar’s flagship model were slightly thicker than those sold to Longyao, reaching fifteen microns, they were still far below the twenty-five-micron safety standard required in the North American market.","In simulated testing, the batteries began to swell at sixty degrees Celsius. At eighty degrees, separator shrinkage caused a short circuit, with the probability of ignition reaching as high as twenty-three percent.","Twenty-three percent.","That meant one out of every four Twostar phones using that batch of batteries could potentially catch fire in a high-temperature environment.","Once this data was made public, the three million Twostar phones in the North American market became the equivalent of three million walking time bombs.","The Consumer Product Safety Commission responded faster than expected.","Just three days later, a stern formal investigative letter was sent from Washington to Twostar Electronics headquarters. The company was ordered to submit complete production records, quality-control reports, and supply-chain traceability information for that batch of batteries within seventy-two hours. Failure to comply would trigger a mandatory recall.","The news sent North America’s tech industry into an uproar.","The Wall Street Journal, The New York Times, The Washington Post, and other major media outlets followed up with reports almost simultaneously.","“Twostar Phones Found to Have Serious Battery Safety Risks, Hundreds of Thousands of Users Face Fire Hazards”","“From the Long Kingdom to North America: Twostar’s Battery Scandal Goes Global”","“Three Million Time Bombs: Twostar May Face the Largest Recall in Its History”","Soon afterward, consumers in multiple states launched a class-action lawsuit against Twostar.","The law firm leading the case was none other than a prestigious firm with a formidable track record, secretly backed by Jesse of the Xuanhuang Society’s North American branch.","The complaint ran more than four hundred pages. It listed more than a dozen charges, including product liability, consumer fraud, negligent infliction of harm, and violations of the commercial codes of various states. The plaintiffs were seeking tens of billions of dollars in damages.","Twostar headquarters, the chairman’s office.","The air seemed to have been sucked out of the room. An oppressive silence filled the office.","Mr. Lee, the head of Twostar Electronics, held the report in his hands, the veins on his forehead bulging.","“Who’s going to tell me what the hell happened?!”","Seven or eight core executives stood in the office, but not one of them dared to make a sound.","They had, of course, known about the reduced-thickness battery separators in the batteries supplied to Longyao.","After Longyao and the Domestic Pride Alliance had been established, the domestic smartphone manufacturers had risen far faster than anyone had anticipated. Twostar’s market share in the Long Kingdom had been rapidly eroded, and someone below had proposed turning up the pressure on Longyao.","Taking advantage of Twostar’s dominance in the battery supply chain, they would supply Longyao with a special batch of batteries. Once Longyao’s products suffered a safety incident, they could dump all the blame on Longyao for inadequate quality control.","This tactic wasn’t new to them. They had used similar methods against small manufacturers in the East Continent before, and it had worked every time.","Even when those small manufacturers discovered problems with the batteries, they had no ability to prove their innocence. In the end, they could only swallow their anger and bear the loss in silence.","But they had severely underestimated the “small manufacturer” known as Longyao.","Not only had Longyao completed an entire series of battery thermal-stability tests within just a few days, it had also arranged for people in the United States to launch a lawsuit.","Combined with the full refunds on 4.2 million phones, the move had ignited public opinion throughout the Long Kingdom. It had backed Twostar into a corner while triggering large-scale sanctions against the company, causing its products to lose nearly ninety percent of their market share overnight.","This time, Twostar had truly kicked an iron plate.","No—damn it, it had kicked a steel plate.","“Chairman, the class-action lawsuit in the United States has officially been filed. If... if we lose, the damages could exceed five billion dollars.”","Mr. Lee suddenly picked up the report and slammed it hard onto the desk.","In the end, he gritted his teeth and said, “Initiate a recall. Recall every phone sold in the US market!”","“Chairman! The cost of recalling all three million phones would be astronomical.”","“You think I’m asking for your opinion?”","“Recall them, or wait for a fifty-billion-dollar damages verdict. You choose.”","The direct cost of recalling three million phones would be astronomical, and the damage to the brand’s reputation would be enormous as well. But at this point, Twostar had no other choice.","“Then... what about the Long Kingdom? Should we recall the phones there too?”","“Recall them in the Long Kingdom? What the hell for? When have we ever recalled a product there?”","“Yes...”"]},{"number":915,"title":"Chapter 915: 916, Duck Pear Phone, triggered.","paragraphs":["Mingzhu City, Tianyi Law Firm.","Zhao Tianyi sat in front of his computer, leisurely browsing overseas media coverage of the Two-Star recall incident.","“Redirecting the blame worked. Now, where should I redirect it next?”","He pushed up his glasses, then pulled out a new industrial design patent. A playful look crossed his face.","“Oh, this is interesting.”","“What’s the saying again? ‘All designs under heaven are copied’? Mr. Jobs, you couldn’t even copy it properly.”","Two days later.","Dressed in a gray polo shirt, flip-flops, and a pair of old-fashioned black-rimmed glasses, Zhao Tianyi looked like an ordinary laborer as he appeared outside Huaqiangbei Electronics Market.","“This place really is the best. If you want to make a phone, you can make it here.”","With both hands stuffed into his pockets, he strolled into Huaqiangbei Electronics Market.","What kind of place was Huaqiangbei?","It was the largest electronics distribution center in the Dragon Kingdom—and the world’s biggest incubator for knockoff phones.","As long as you could produce a design drawing, you could have a phone assembled here within three days that looked exactly like the genuine article.","Zhao Tianyi had come for one simple reason: to hand over the exterior design plans for the Fruit 5.","More precisely, he had come to give the knockoff manufacturers of Huaqiangbei the Fruit 5 exterior-patent drawings that he had registered in advance.","The whole thing was rather absurd.","Last year, the patent battle between the Longyao S1 and the Fruit 4 had caused a huge uproar. Everyone on the internet knew that Fruit had copied Longyao’s design.","Mr. Jobs’s team had kept their heads down for an entire year and finally produced the Fruit 5. They had completely revamped the exterior, lengthening the body, enlarging the screen from 3.5 inches to 4 inches, and changing the back to a three-section design combining metal and glass. They thought they had finally avoided any chance of a clash.","But what happened?","The Young Lady had already had the elongated-phone design registered a year earlier.","That was called anticipating your anticipation.","The Fruit design team probably never imagined that the new exterior they had painstakingly refined in the laboratory had already been patented a year in advance before the drawings had even left the building.","There ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​‍was nothing they could do. Someone was using a cheat code.","Even though the Fruit 5’s exterior in his previous life could not possibly have been exactly the same as it was now, the general direction certainly would not change.","An elongated body, a three-section back panel, thinner bezels... As long as those design elements were registered ahead of time, Fruit’s path could be blocked completely.","But this time, what the Young Lady intended to do was even more ruthless than last year.","Last year, she had waited until Fruit released the phone before filing a lawsuit. This year, she planned to flood Huaqiangbei with knockoff phones before Fruit even held its launch event.","When Mr. Jobs took the Fruit 5 out onstage, the reporters in the audience would all pull out knockoffs that looked exactly the same. Just imagining that scene was enough to make one whistle in admiration.","Zhao Tianyi had to admit that the Young Lady’s move was brilliant. But then again, this was often what business warfare looked like—simple and brutally effective.","All it took was one exterior-design patent to drive a world-class manufacturer completely insane.","Zhao Tianyi soon strolled into a small workshop specializing in high-end knockoff phones.","The owner was a balding man in his forties. He was squatting on the floor with a cigarette between his teeth, taking apart a phone of some unknown brand.","“Boss, interested in doing some business?” Zhao Tianyi pulled a USB drive from his pocket.","The bald owner looked up and sized him up. “What kind of business?”","“I have the exterior design plans for the latest Fruit 5, and I have the patent as well. Take a look and see if you’re interested.” Zhao Tianyi handed the USB drive to him.","The owner’s eyes immediately lit up. He plugged the drive into the computer and opened the design file.","A 360-degree rotating rendering of a phone appeared on the screen.","A four-inch display, a three-section metal back panel, and a brand-new Lightning port at the bottom. The entire body was noticeably longer than the Fruit 4.","The bald owner’s previously casual expression changed instantly.","“This... this is real?”","“Of course it’s real. It’s the design for the new phone—the Fruit 5 that was just leaked.” Zhao Tianyi deliberately glanced around before lowering his voice. “I have a friend who works in Fruit’s design department. He risked his life to get this out, and he even registered the patent in advance. Take a look. Can you make it?”","The bald owner’s eyes nearly popped out of his head.","The Fruit 5’s design plans!","For a phone that had not even been released yet!","He had been making knockoffs for many years, but this was the first time he had gotten the genuine product’s design before its official launch.","If he could start shipping ahead of everyone else, wouldn’t he make a fortune?","“Brother, there won’t be any problems with this, will there?” The bald owner swallowed hard.","“The patent is included. What are you worried about? There are even 3D modeling files and the mold parameters. You can take them straight to production.”","“I don’t want much. Just ten thousand.”","“Ten thousand?” The bald owner thought he had misheard.","These were the design plans for Fruit’s unreleased new phone, complete with a patent. On the black market, they would be worth at least several hundred thousand. Yet this man only wanted ten thousand.","“Brother, are you sure you only want ten thousand?”","Zhao Tianyi nodded. “That’s right. I just want to get it into production as soon as possible. Keeping this thing is a liability.”","“If you think it’s too expensive, I’ll find someone else.”","“Not expensive, not expensive!” Afraid that Zhao Tianyi might change his mind, the bald owner hurriedly counted out ten thousand yuan in cash from a drawer and stuffed it into his hands. “If you get any more good stuff like this, remember to come to me first!”","Zhao Tianyi shoved the cash into his pocket and turned to leave.","He then visited more than twenty other knockoff workshops using exactly the same method.","More than twenty USB drives were handed out, and the Fruit 5’s exterior design spread through Huaqiangbei’s underground network like a virus.","Three days later.","The first batch of Fruit 5 knockoffs appeared on the counters of Huaqiangbei.","They were priced at just 699 yuan.","From the front, they looked exactly like Fruit’s soon-to-be-released new phone.","From the side, they looked exactly the same.","Turn one over and the back was identical too.","The only difference was the logo on the back: a pear with a bite taken out of it. In every other respect, it was a perfect replica.","Well, “perfect replica” might be overstating things. After all, the knockoff ran on Android, so the interface looked a little different once the phone was turned on.","But as far as the exterior was concerned, it had achieved a pixel-perfect level of imitation.","News of the knockoffs quickly spread online, accompanied by an especially shameless advertisement:","“America has Fruit; the Dragon Kingdom has Pear! Pear Phone—the fighter jet of phones. Let’s go!”","The moment the news broke, digital forums exploded.","“What the hell? Huaqiangbei already has the Fruit 5? The launch event hasn’t even happened yet!”","“I’m dying. The genuine Fruit hasn’t even been released, and the knockoff is already on sale.”","“699 yuan for a Fruit 5? Huaqiangbei is incredible!”","“What do you mean Fruit 5? They clearly said it’s a Pear Phone.”","“I don’t know whether it’s a pear or not, but I do know that Fruit must be under enormous pressure right now.”","“Jobs must be devastated. This is the second time, right?”","“...”","America...","Jobs was standing in the lounge backstage at the launch event, making the final preparations before the presentation.","An hour later, the launch of the Fruit 5 would be broadcast live worldwide from the Moscone Convention Center.","They had prepared thoroughly this time and were confident that nothing could go wrong.","Last year, the Fruit 4 had been left red-faced by Longyao’s design patent, and it had infuriated him.","This year, he had learned his lesson. More than six months in advance, he had ordered the design team to create an entirely new exterior. The body was longer, the screen was larger, and the back featured a three-section metal construction. Overall, the design was noticeably different from that of the Fruit 4.","Surely no one would accuse them of copying this time, right?","Jobs had even already imagined the lines he would deliver at the presentation: “The Fruit 5 features a truly original design that belongs to Fruit. It represents an entirely new breakthrough in industrial aesthetics!”","At the thought, the corners of Jobs’s mouth lifted slightly. He picked up the coffee on the table and took a sip.","Just then, the lounge door was suddenly shoved open, and the company’s legal director rushed in, his face almost completely drained of color.","“Mr. Jobs!”","“Something terrible has happened!”","Jobs frowned. “What’s got you so worked up?”","The legal director quickly opened a video on his laptop and showed it to him.","Jobs glanced down at the screen, and his smile instantly froze.","It was a product demonstration of a mobile phone.","A four-inch screen, a three-section metal back, and a new port at the bottom—it was exactly the same as the Fruit 5 he was about to unveil.","The only difference was the logo on the back: a pear with a bite taken out of it.","“What... what is this?”","“A knockoff phone from Huaqiangbei in the Dragon Kingdom. They’ve already produced and put large quantities of them on the market.”","“Mr. Jobs, that’s not even the worst part. The worst part is that, just like last year, someone registered the design patent for the Fruit 5 ahead of us. Their application date was a full nine months earlier than ours.”","The lounge fell silent.","A few seconds later, Jobs exploded.","Bang!","He smashed the coffee cup violently onto the floor and roared furiously:","“Fire everyone in the design department! Every last one of them!”"]},{"number":916,"title":"Chapter 916: 917. The Wanlong Society headquarters is completed, and a ribbon-cutting ceremony is held.","paragraphs":["While Fruit was still tearing his hair out over the counterfeit-phone problem,","Longguo, Pearl City.","The sky was a brilliant blue, with wispy clouds drifting across it—a rare day of perfect weather.","A convoy of more than a hundred black Mercedes-Benz sedans moved slowly along a broad, two-way, six-lane road.","Leading the convoy was a black Maybach.","On either side of the road, a young man in a black suit stood every ten meters. Each wore a silver dragon-shaped insignia on his chest.","They stood ramrod straight, their hands clasped behind their backs and their gazes fixed straight ahead, forming a wall of black.","The ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌‌‍convoy came to a slow stop at the end of the road.","The car doors opened, and Liu Yutong stepped out of the Maybach.","She was once again dressed in a tailored black suit, paired with a white silk blouse. A pure-gold dragon-shaped insignia was pinned to her chest.","Before her stood a vast complex of brand-new buildings.","Three silver-gray towers with glass curtain walls stood in a triangular formation, connected by overhead walkways. They looked like three enormous swords pulled from the earth and thrust straight into the blue sky.","Atop the towers stood a massive sign bearing the words “Wanlong Association.”","Centered around the three towers, the complex extended outward in three concentric rings.","The innermost ring was the central office district. The middle ring housed research and development facilities and data centers.","The outer ring was dedicated to employee life and recreation, including staff apartments, a fitness center, employee cafeterias, a library, and an ecological park covering nearly a hundred mu.","At the center of the park was an artificial lake with crystal-blue water. Ginkgo and cherry trees had been planted all around its shores.","Farther away stood a regulation soccer field, an indoor basketball arena, and a massive martial arts hall.","A dragon-shaped insignia was carved into the roof of the martial arts hall as well, giving it an imposing presence.","This was the new headquarters of the Wanlong Association Group, built over more than three years: the Wanlong Association Central Headquarters.","After several rounds of expansion and adjustments, the complex covered more than two thousand mu, with a total floor area exceeding two million square meters. It could accommodate as many as one hundred thousand people working and living there at the same time—essentially a small city within the city.","Liu Yutong stood in the central plaza enclosed by the three main towers, gazing up at the complex that belonged to her.","Behind her stood a group of Wanlong Association veterans who had followed The Young Lady all the way from Wushui County.","Nearly everyone was filled with pride as they looked upon the immense complex.","Four years.","From a rented farmhouse in Wushui County, to office space in Shunchang Tower in Pearl City, and finally to this sprawling, two-thousand-mu headquarters—they had followed The Young Lady, advancing one step at a time and painstakingly building a business empire that could rival any world-class corporation.","Everyone stood there for a long time, reluctant to leave.","It was only when Yun Cheng reminded her from the side that they finally stirred.","“The Young Lady, the auspicious hour has arrived.”","Liu Yutong nodded, withdrew her gaze, and turned toward the ribbon-cutting ceremony.","The ribbon-cutting stage had been set up directly in front of the central plaza, enclosed by the three main towers. Behind it stood a massive relief wall carved with a dragon motif.","A golden dragon coiled across nearly the entire wall. Its head was held high, its eyes wide open as it looked down over the plaza, radiating grandeur and power.","Quite a number of people were already standing on the stage.","Many of Pearl City’s leaders had come, along with several key provincial officials. The scale and prestige of the gathering were absolutely unprecedented among private enterprises in Pearl City.","The business guests were no less illustrious.","Pony Ma, chairman of Big Goose Group; Ma Yunyun, chairman of Ali Group; Lei Jobs, founder of Rice Technology; Ji Zhe, founding partner of Qixing Capital; Chu Hai, head of AEG Capital’s Longguo division; and several tycoons from Harbor City—the mere mention of any one of them could make the entire business world of Longguo tremble.","Members of the Yushan Society had also come.","After several rounds of expansion, the Yushan Society now had more than thirty members, all children of top-tier aristocratic families or wealthy clans.","There were overseas guests as well. Jesse and Bai Shisui had personally flown back with members of the Overseas Chamber of Commerce and the Xuanhuang Society to attend the ribbon-cutting ceremony. A group of them stood on the stage in sharp suits, making the scene especially lively.","Liu Yutong walked to the front of the stage and shook hands with the leaders one by one.","When she reached the senior local official, he could not resist chatting with her for a little longer.","“Director Liu, congratulations!”","“The completion of the Wanlong Association Central Headquarters is not only a joyous occasion for the Wanlong Association Group, but also for Pearl City. It is a milestone in the economic development of our entire city.”","“You’re too kind, Senior Official Gao.”","“Without the support of the leadership, the Wanlong Association Central Headquarters could never have been completed so quickly.”","“Ah, Director Liu, you’re being too modest.”","“The Wanlong Association Group is Pearl City’s largest private enterprise, as well as one of our city’s calling cards. Your achievements are our achievements, and your glory is Pearl City’s glory.”","At that point, his tone suddenly shifted.","“Director Liu, speaking of that, I just remembered something. You once mentioned to me that Pearl City would eventually have an airport, didn’t you? I’ve kept those words in mind all this time.”","Liu Yutong smiled at his words.","It was a long story.","As a prefecture-level city, Pearl City had never had a civilian airport of its own. For years, residents who wanted to take a flight had to travel to a neighboring city—two hours by car or three hours by bus—which was extremely inconvenient.","Senior Official Gao had submitted countless reports on the matter. The authorities had also sent people to inspect the area several times, but there had never been any definite news.","That was until the day at the stadium, when Liu Yutong happened to discuss the matter with him.","From then on, Senior Official Gao’s hopes had never faded. His term in office was also drawing to a close, and he would probably be transferred soon. Before leaving, he wanted to resolve this long-standing concern and give the several million people of Pearl City an answer.","“Senior Official Gao, an airport is the shared hope of Pearl City’s several million residents, as well as an inevitable necessity for the city’s development.”","“I think we should be hearing some news before long,” Liu Yutong said.","Senior Official Gao’s smile grew even brighter.","“Director Liu, the people of Pearl City will remember this kindness.”","“You’re making too much of it. The Wanlong Association’s roots are in Pearl City. Anything that concerns Pearl City concerns the Wanlong Association.”","After exchanging pleasantries with the officials and distinguished guests, Liu Yutong walked with them to the center of the ribbon-cutting stage.","A ceremonial hostess came forward carrying a tray. Resting on the red velvet was a pair of golden scissors.","Liu Yutong took the scissors. Then, in full view of tens of thousands of Wanlong Association core members and ordinary employees, as well as more than a hundred heavyweight guests from the political and business worlds, she brought the blades down decisively.","Snip.","The red ribbon fell apart.","Thunderous applause erupted and continued without end.","The Wanlong Association Central Headquarters had officially opened."]},{"number":917,"title":"Chapter 917: 918, Booth passes away.","paragraphs":["Apple headquarters, United States.","After a period of internal restructuring, Apple 5 had laid off a large number of designers and gone through months of turmoil. In the end, the company decided to hold the launch event as planned and release the new phone as scheduled.","After all, they had already invested enormous sums in the preparations. Advertising campaigns, supply-chain production schedules, launch venues booked in dozens of countries and regions around the world... Real money had been poured into all of it.","If they canceled everything at the last minute because of a batch of knockoff phones from Huaqiangbei, the losses would be impossible to estimate.","They had finally seen through the other side’s particularly disgusting strategy.","Put simply, their opponent had never intended to fight Apple in court. What they wanted was to use a knockoff phone to go head-to-head with Apple and destroy the value of its brand.","After his initial fury, Jobs quickly calmed down.","That very night, he summoned all of Apple’s senior executives and held a six-hour closed-door meeting in the company’s headquarters conference room.","Outsiders never learned the specifics of the meeting. However, according to a former Apple executive who later spoke about it privately, Jobs said only a few words at the end.","“Hold the launch event as planned.”","“The design of Apple 5 will not change.”","“As for that Pear phone or whatever it is... have the legal department deal with it.”","Jobs’s reasoning was simple.","Although the appearance of Apple 5 had been patented by someone else in advance, this situation was different from what had happened with Apple 4 the previous year.","Last year, Apple 4 had directly collided with the exterior design of Longyao S1. Longyao was, at the very least, a well-known brand with a major company backing it, which made the matter extremely troublesome to resolve.","This time, although Apple 5 and the Pear phone had similarly identical designs, what exactly was the Pear phone? A knockoff manufactured in Huaqiangbei. It had no legitimate sales channels and no brand recognition whatsoever. How could it possibly go up against Apple?","Apple could easily turn the accusation around, claim that the other side had maliciously registered the patent, and even sue them for unfair competition.","Of course, there was another, even more important reason Jobs dared to take such a hard line.","The United States had already begun preparing to make its move.","The U.S. Department of Commerce had quietly launched an export-control investigation targeting Chinese technology companies. The investigation covered more than a dozen key sectors, including chips, operating systems, high-end sensors, and precision instruments.","Although the official control list had not yet been released, everyone in the industry already knew that once it went into effect, every Chinese phone manufacturer that relied heavily on imported chips would suffer.","As for the LX-A1 chip inside the Longyao S1, although it had been independently developed by Longxin, its ARM architecture license, EDA design tools, and some of its semiconductor manufacturing equipment all came from the West.","In other words, Longyao’s lifeline had always been in America’s hands.","Jobs believed that as long as the United States tightened its export controls even slightly, Longyao and the so-called National Champions Alliance would soon fall apart.","By then, who would care about some exterior-design patent? Who would even remember the Pear phone?","That was exactly what he thought.","What Jobs never could have imagined, however, was that he would never live to see that day.","August 6.","A piece of news exploded across the global technology industry like a bomb.","Apple officially announced that Jobs, the company’s co-founder and former CEO, had died of illness on the afternoon of August 5 local time.","The news sent shock waves around the world.","Whether in the West or the East, nearly every major media outlet put the story on its front page and led its news broadcasts with it.","“An Era Comes to an End.”","“He Changed the World—More Than Once.”","“Apple Has Lost Its Soul. Silicon Valley Has Lost Its Guiding Light.”","“.........”","The reaction in China was just as explosive.","Seven of the top ten trending topics on Weibo were related to Jobs.","#JobsDies was marked with a bright red “Breaking” label.","#AppleFounderDiesOfIllness — Trending!","#PancreaticCancer — Trending!","#China’sTechIndustryMournsCollectively — Hot!","#YuXinPostsTributeToJobs — Hot!","#TheGrudgeBetweenLongyaoAndApple — Trending!","#WasJobsAngeredToDeath???#","As soon as the final topic appeared, the comments section instantly fell apart.","Before that, countless users had been mourning Jobs of their own accord.","“Fifty-six years old. Far too young. A cruel twist of fate.”","“I use a Longyao phone, but I have to admit that Jobs was a great innovator. He changed phones, music, animated films... He changed so many things.”","“The patent battle between Apple 4 and Longyao S1 still hasn’t been settled, and now Jobs is gone. Life is unpredictable.”","“May he rest in peace.”","But the mourning did not last long. As soon as the final trending topic appeared, the tone of the comments changed.","It began on foreign social media.","“Was Jobs driven to his death by the Chinese?”","“Think about it. Last year, Apple 4 was humiliated by Longyao’s exterior-design patent, and the whole world mocked Apple for copying a Chinese design. Jobs was such a proud man. How could he possibly endure that kind of humiliation?”","“Apple ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌‍5 was just about to launch this year, and then knockoffs from Huaqiangbei started flooding the market—and they even came with exterior-design patents. Can you believe it? A knockoff phone with a design patent?”","“Jobs spent an entire year preparing that launch event, only for it to become another joke.”","“Exactly! The Chinese kept riding roughshod over him. Who could take that kind of abuse? Jobs was already in poor health. Being pushed that far must have accelerated the deterioration of his condition.”","“And Chinese companies have the nerve to issue condolences? They should be hauled before an international court.”","“Boycott Chinese phones! Boycott Longyao! Boycott the Wanlong Alliance! Boycott everything made in China!”","“...........”","These comments spread like a virus across foreign social media.","The foreign media quickly caught the scent and jumped in to fan the flames.","The Wall Street Journal published a commentary titled “Jobs and China: An Unequal War.”","The article devoted considerable space to recounting the battle over exterior-design patents between Apple and the Wanlong Alliance. Then, in a seemingly objective tone laced with insinuation, it wrote:","“During the final two years of his life, Jobs was forced to confront a series of relentless challenges from China’s most aggressive technology companies. These challenges took place not only on the commercial front, but also struck at the very core of his pride as an innovator. For a man who regarded design as a faith, being accused of plagiarism was undoubtedly the heaviest blow imaginable. We cannot determine whether these pressures accelerated the deterioration of his illness, but the coincidence in timing inevitably invites speculation.”","Other media outlets quickly followed suit.","“Jobs’s Final Battle—His Opponent: China’s Wanlong Alliance”","“The Cruelest Psychological Warfare in Business History”","“The Wolf-Pack Tactics of Chinese Companies Are Destroying the Global Innovation Ecosystem”","“Exclusive Interview with a Takahashi Conglomerate Executive—The Unfair Competitive Practices of Chinese Technology Companies”","Within just a few days, public opinion had shifted from mourning Jobs to condemning Chinese technology companies from every direction.","And the Wanlong Association Group was bearing the brunt of it.","A few days later.","Mingzhu City, Wanlong Association Group Headquarters.","Yu Xin had just come out of a research and development meeting for the Longyao S2 when her assistant came over with some troubling news.","“President Yu, there’s a large group of reporters blocking the entrance. They’re all here for you.”","“For me?”","“Yes. The public sentiment online has become very abnormal.”","“Foreign social media is full of conspiracy theories claiming that Jobs was driven to his death by us. Foreign media outlets have also joined in, deliberately fanning the flames. Some domestic media are beginning to repost the stories as well. The public relations department has managed to suppress a batch of them, but it can’t keep up.”","Yu Xin was rendered speechless. What was this supposed to be?","But she also understood that Wanlong Association was bound to face a day like this sooner or later.","After all, once you reached a high enough position, it was impossible to avoid being watched from every direction. There would be praise, envy, malice—every kind of attention imaginable.","There was no hiding from it.","“Let’s go. I’ll meet them.”","Outside the lobby on the first floor of Wanlong Association’s headquarters, more than a hundred reporters had gathered in a dense crowd.","The moment Yu Xin appeared at the entrance, camera flashes erupted like a torrential downpour, so intense that they were nearly impossible to look through.","“President Yu, foreign media outlets claim that Jobs was driven to his death by your company. What do you have to say?”","“President Yu, Longyao has used design patents to target Apple for two consecutive years. Does that constitute malicious competition?”","“There are reports that Wanlong Association clashed with local gangs in San Francisco years ago. Is that true?”","“Is Wanlong Association really a legitimate company?”","“President Yu, please answer our questions!”","“......”"]},{"number":918,"title":"Chapter 918: 919, Super Financial Conglomerate + Super Syndicate","paragraphs":["Yu Xin stood on the steps, facing hundreds of microphones and cameras. Her expression was perfectly calm.","She waited until the reporters had finished firing off their questions before speaking.","“Mr. Jobs was a great innovator, and history will remember his contributions. Apple set a benchmark for the global technology industry, and Mr. Jobs himself was a senior figure I have always respected. On behalf of the Wanlong Association Group and Longyao Technology, I would like to express our deepest condolences on his passing.”","Then she changed tack.","“As for the conspiracy theories claiming that we angered Mr. Jobs to death, all I can say is this: If we really had that kind of power, Longyao would have become the number-one company in the world a long time ago.”","“If that were really the case, would we still need to work so hard on research and development? Of course not. We’d simply anger the founders of all our competitors one by one, and that would do the trick.”","The moment she said this, the reporters at the scene burst out laughing.","“But there are people online saying that the Wanlong Association’s methods go beyond business,” an overseas reporter said. “Some even claim that you used improper methods in the United States—for example, sending criminal organizations to XXX. What do you have to say about that, Ms. Yu?”","Yu Xin looked at the foreign reporter and replied sarcastically, “People tend to judge others by their own standards. Clearly, those making these accusations are fond of such methods themselves, which is why they assume the Wanlong Association would do the same.”","“Let me emphasize this once again: the Wanlong Association has always been a legitimate Chinese company that obeys the law.”","“If anyone believes we have done anything illegal, they are welcome to provide evidence. Our legal department is ready to meet them in court at any time.”","The moment she finished that last sentence, the eyes of the men in black standing behind her instantly turned sharp.","The pressure they exuded frightened several of the reporters standing closest to them so badly that they did not dare ask another question.","Yu Xin smiled and nodded at the reporters before turning and heading back into the building.","The men in black behind her followed in perfect formation.","The reporters exchanged glances.","A legitimate company?","When you say you’re legitimate, could you at least stop the men behind you from looking at us as if they’re deciding which of us to kill first?","It’s terrifying!","The video of Yu Xin’s response was soon uploaded online.","Most Chinese netizens reacted in much the same way.","“Ms. Yu is so badass! That’s exactly how you should answer those foreign media outlets.”","“Jobs had pancreatic cancer for years. Foreign media reported several times before that he was critically ill. Now that he’s gone, they’re blaming Longyao? Western media really are hypocrites.”","“Wanlong Association Legal Department warning: If you claim we angered someone to death, please provide a medical report.”","“Hahahaha, I’m dying. Did anyone else notice the expressions of those men in black behind Ms. Yu while she was speaking? They genuinely looked like they wanted to beat those rumor-mongering reporters to death on the spot.”","“Don’t make things up. They’re a legitimate company. How could they possibly do something like that? At most, they’d send the legal department to have a private chat with you.”","“Legal Department: Chat my ass. We’re going straight to court!”","“Enough already. Let Jobs’ death rest. The dead deserve respect. Stop joining in with the foreign media’s rabble-rousing.”","“..........”","However, the rational discussion taking place in China did nothing to stop the conspiracy theories overseas from gaining momentum.","On Twitter, troublemakers began widely reposting screenshots of old news articles from the first time members of the Wanlong Association arrived in San Francisco. They also turned various rumors into sensational headlines.","Claims that San Francisco’s underground forces had been wiped out by the Wanlong Association. Stories about the terrifying Hell Giant. Rumors surrounding the mysterious Black Phoenix.","All sorts of long-forgotten events were dug up.","One person even wrote a five-thousand-word post dedicated to exposing this unusual Chinese company.","“The Chinese Super-Society: The Birth of the Wanlong Association.”","The post began with the Wanlong Association’s origins in Wushui County and traced its rise all the way to Pearl City. It even listed, in painstaking detail, the downfall of underworld bosses in several Chinese provinces, the details of multiple battles for control of corporate shares, the Goose Group acquisition, the founding of the National Products Pride Alliance, and more.","Some of the information was true and could be verified. Some of it had supposedly been gathered by sending people out to make inquiries, while the rest was nothing more than hearsay.","But because the post was written in such convincing detail, readers were left stunned.","“This is insane. The Wanlong Association’s rise has been way too fast—and they’re so dark!”","The post also devoted an entire section to how the Wanlong Association had supposedly wiped out San Francisco’s local gangs in its early years, along with tales of the terrifying Hell Giant and other legends. It portrayed them as a gigantic criminal organization disguised as a corporation.","“My God. After reading this post, I’ve realized that the Wanlong Association isn’t an ordinary company at all. It’s a society empire wearing a corporate disguise.”","“Jobs died in a hospital bed, while his rival acquired the Goose Group, sanctioned Samsung, and drove Apple into a corner all within a single month. And now you’re telling me that’s a coincidence? Sorry, I don’t buy it.”","“A company capable of breaking through Apple’s defenses, swallowing the Goose Group, and blacklisting Samsung in just two years must have some extraordinary backing.”","“I have a friend who’s a Wall Street analyst. He says the amount of capital controlled by the Wanlong Association may be far greater than what we can see on the surface. What we’re seeing now may only be the tip of the iceberg.”","“So this is the Chinese version of a mafia conglomerate? And they don’t seem satisfied with ruling their own country anymore. Now they’re preparing to expand overseas.”","“What’s even more frightening is their founder—the woman they call ‘The Young Lady.’ She’s only twenty-two this year. She’s an absolute monster.”","“I also looked into their company badges. They have different ranks. Silver is for ordinary members, platinum is for executives, and there’s only one pure-gold badge—the one belonging to The Young Lady. Isn’t that exactly how a criminal organization’s hierarchy works?”","“The scariest part is that they even hold martial arts tournaments internally. I saw leaked footage of the competitions. Every one of those people looked vicious, and their strikes were fast and brutal. And you’re telling me this is a legitimate company? Not even a ghost would believe that.”","“Even if Jobs wasn’t angered to death by them, after reading all this, I believe they’re criminals.”","“..........”","The rumors grew more outrageous with every retelling.","From Jobs’ death to the Wanlong Association’s overseas expansion; from the Dragon Soaring Cup martial arts tournament to the hierarchy of its dragon-shaped badges; from its convoy of hundreds of Mercedes-Benz vehicles to the global operations of the Black Phoenix Society—bits and pieces of information were cobbled together in the minds of Western netizens, creating a vast, mysterious, and terrifying image.","A frightening fusion of a Chinese super-conglomerate and a criminal empire.","Although ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​‍most of the claims were merely speculation and conjecture, with little concrete evidence to support them, the less evidence there was, the more outrageous the conspiracy theories became.","The Wanlong Association’s reputation overseas grew darker—and louder—with every passing day."]}]);
